    ("18.4268", "★★★★ job producer chain root-caused: the appTouch/input event-poll thread 0x40017 starts but finds an empty event list and idles, so no touch data ever reaches FUN_81174CD4 and no job is ever posted; (1) decoded thread argument blocks (THRARG now prints 4 words) tid=40017000 w1=811F22B9 -> thread 0x40017 runs FUN_811F22B8 the input event-poll thread; tid=40018000/40019000 w1=811732FF w2=00000001 w3=8485815C/848997BC -> the two appJobQueue drain threads (0x811732FF drain loop, w3 queue object) matching old-runtime THREAD argblk [4]=0x811732FF; (2) new probes TOUCHPROD at 0x811F22B8 and POSTCB at 0x81174CD4: DEFAULT 30M TOUCHPROD=1 (thread starts r0=r1=0), POSTCB=0 JOBPOST=0 JOBFN=0 TOUCH=0; HOST-THREAD 5M TOUCHPROD=0 (thread never starts in this mode); (3) disassembly FUN_811F22B8 infinite poll loop r6=[0x81539754] input context, r5=[r6+0xC] pending-event list head; if r5==0 DelayThread(0x1388=5000us) loop; when event exists calls 0x811F0B82 event dispatch per node, unlinks/updates list ([r5+0x20]/[r5+0x24], [r6+0x10]/[r6+0xC]), decrements [r4+0x2C]/[r8+0xFBC], loops; nothing ever posted into [0x81539754]+0xC in our run so poll thread idles every 5ms touch never reaches FUN_81174CD4 job queue A stays empty drain threads poll head=0 (M722); default 30M stable exit=0 BADMEM=0 GXM=12 FSW=16; NEXT find producer of input-event queue object [0x81539754]+0xC (list insert site 0x811F231C-0x811F2362 in this function queue-manipulation code; posting path mirror routine elsewhere) probe 0x81539754 and writers compare old-runtime log/appInput-module call sites candidates HLE touch/ctrl event injection (SceCtrl poll guest-pull only, SceTouch poll-based now) or guest thread 0x40016/others that should synthesize input events; once one event posted chain should light up FUN_811F22B8 -> 0x811F0B82 -> FUN_81174CD4 -> FUN_81003CCC -> enqueue FUN_8101603C -> job fn 0x81003D89 -> sceTouchRead 0x812B1930 implemented M721."),
    ("18.4267", "★★★★ appJobQueue probes added: drain consumers alive and polling but no job ever posted - posting chain is appTouch -> FUN_81174CD4 -> thunk 0x81003B72 -> FUN_81003CCC -> enqueue FUN_8101603C; probes JOBPOST at enqueue call block 0x81003D26, JOBFN at job fn 0x81003D88, JOBQ at consumer entry 0x810160E8, ENQ at list insert 0x810160C4, QHEAD at dequeue 0x810160FC hooked into host-thread loop and all five fiber/main dispatch loops; DEFAULT 30M JOBQ=2 (threads 0x40018/0x40019 enter drain loops q=0x848580BC/q=0x8489971C), QHEAD=20 all polls head=0, but JOBPOST=0 ENQ=0 JOBFN=0 TOUCH=0 - consumers armed and polling empty queues no job ever enters; HOST-THREAD 5M JOBQ=0 drain consumers never enter loops in this mode (stop earlier at event-flag wait); posting chain resolved FUN_81003CCC head (takes job object r0, calls 0x81003BA0, copies fields [r6+0xAC..] into queue slots, calls enqueue FUN_8101603C with queue pointer from global [0x81328B00], job fn 0x81003D89, arg r4) <- thunk FUN_81003B72 (call 0x81003B74) <- FUN_81174CD4 (call 0x81174CE6; module range 0x81174B02-0x81174CBE appTouch/appTouch_module_gfd); first job originates from appTouch input processing; job fn 0x81003D89 begins with sceTouchRead 0x812B1930 and branches to assert path if return !=1 - M721 sceTouchRead implementation exactly on this path not exercised yet; cross-check old runtime h145k91 log JOBPOST~6804/JOBFN~6500 then stopped while early run.log only reaches DEQ/JOBDRAIN-WAIT L686-708 with no JOBPOST - same early-boot shape as our run; job posting requires reaching appTouch sampling which boot stall prevents; default 30M stable exit=0 BADMEM=0 GXM=12 FSW=16 host-thread 5M exit=0 BADMEM=0; NEXT probe FUN_81174CD4/call site 0x81174CE6 and appTouch sampling state machine 0x8117339C-0x81174AB2 find gating condition preventing first post tie to main wait node state 0x811E5EC2/0x84CF3E70 state!=6 or on host-thread path fix why drain consumers never enter loops."),
    ("18.4266", "★★★★ full-text review of the master doc + companion reports yielded a directly usable fix and a clear priority list; implemented the latent P1 landmine sceTouchRead (0x812B1930); (1) code change HLE_DIFF_REPORT.md §2.10/§2.9 marks 0x812B1930 = sceTouchRead NID 0x169A1D58 no case -> returns 0 -> guest hits vita_ll_touch.c:177 assert (old runtime had 6,178 calls returning 1); ported old-runtime authoritative implementation n_touch_read: clear exactly 16 + min(nBuf,8)*0x20 bytes of SceTouchData (16-byte header + nBuf reports) and return nBuf?1:0; report explicit landmine warning honored - never memset 0x140 blindly because nBuf buffer sits right before appJobQueue slot objects and old 0x140 clear corrupted slot[+0] (should be -1) triggering appJobQueue.c:194 assert; new TOUCH probe prints first 8 calls; verified default 30M exit=0 BADMEM=0 GXM=12 FSW=16 host-thread 15M exit=0 BADMEM=0 RDR=5 TOUCH count=0 in both (appJobQueue/touch job path still not reached as expected); (2) document review catalog SCHED_SPIN_ANALYSIS.md root-cause A1-A7 + P0-0 3 probes + P0-A/B/C/D + 2M/30M/100M criteria; OLD_RUNTIME_FIBER_HLE.md old-runtime semantics with line numbers (switch eboot_probe.cpp:6965-6995 / thumb_interpreter.cpp:967-978,11007,11714-11717; sched 7044-7142; DelayThread 7441-7462; fiber_setup 6940-6963; getSelf 6932-6938) + port checklist P0-1/P0-2/P0-3/P1/P2/P3; master doc 18.4212-18.4234 lessons P0-B factbit off P0-C DelayThread every call P0-D GetThreadId TLS object CreateSema/EventFlag r2 arg bug WaitEventFlag bitfield semantics negative results naive pump BADMEM va=8 @0x811C0DA8 LwMutex live-writes corrupt heap SCHEDRUN fake completion; master doc ARCH/h-series appJobQueue map source 0x812EE6A4 appJobQueue.c queues A=0xA038401C sig 0x1A B=0xA03CA01C sig 0x1B twin EFs created at lr=0x811732A0 bt 0x81173172->0x81015F76->0x812EE6A4 producer posts only A via lr=0x81003D2A jobfn 0x81003D89 consumers FUN_810160E8 via trampoline 0x81173308 list insert 0x810160C4-0x810160D2 old runtime JOBPOST~6804 JOBFN~6500 then stopped first HLE sceTouchRead JOBASSERT slot incomplete our 0x40018/19 wait on 0x60014000/15000 == old 0x6008/0x6009 wait 0x1A/0x1B; old log C:/dev/p5d_build/run.log 26751 lines ground truth; HLE_DIFF_REPORT stub priorities TouchRead P1 now fixed; _MODULE_INDEX module ranges appJobQueue 0x81015F24-0x810160E8 appSystem 0x81172EFC-0x811730C2 appTouch 0x8117339C-0x81174AB2 appSound 0x81170CF8-0x81172828; _ASSERT_MAP GXM_ABI_TEST_REPORT P5D_DIGEST 892KB; NEXT (a) add appJobQueue probes JOBPOST/JOBFN/ENQ/DEQ/QHEAD/QEXEC + SCHED_SPIN P0-0 three probes and diff harness timeline against run.log first divergence (b) continue HLE_DIFF_REPORT high-priority stubs touch done audio/NGS etc (c) choose scheduler route with evidence port OLD_RUNTIME_FIBER_HLE single-executor semantics or promote host-thread model already reaches RDR=5/GXP and fix file-entry payload; docs support real-host-thread architecture (d) do not retry naive fiber-world pumping (M720 crash matches documented M685 negative result)."),
    ("18.4265", "★★★★★ found a dead feature: g_thrpump_env (the pump guest worker threads from inside the fiber world switch used by earlier milestones) was NEVER ASSIGNED - there is no getenv P5D_THRPUMP parse in the harness so hle_thr_pump always returns early in default cooperative mode (if g_in_fiber_exec && !g_thrpump_env return) and the worker threads (Gfd/Cri) can never run while main flow is inside app fiber; that is exactly why default run workers stay waiting forever app-init thread never completes and [0x816CC630] never cleared (M719); fixed wiring added missing P5D_THRPUMP env parse (g_thrpump_env = getenv P5D_THRPUMP != 0) and re-tested with P5D_THRPUMP=1 P5D_NESTED_UNTIL=1500000: pump now DOES run from fiber world (THRYIELD DelayThread -> pump thr thr count=7, main loop leaves pure-wait pattern) but run crashes early at n≈260,000 with BADMEM guest va=0x00000000 block=0x811EAAE4 tid=0 stub=812B1BA0 ring saturated 0x811EB04E exit code 3 - naive fiber-world pumping not re-entrancy-safe (nested pump while g_in_fiber_exec, thread contexts run inside fiber machinery corrupt exec/fiber state / run with zero PC); default config without env unchanged and stable 30M exit=0 guest/HLE BADMEM=0 GXM=12 FSW=16; NEXT harden hle_thr_pump for fiber-world calls (a) pump depth/re-entrancy guard (b) save/restore g_in_fiber_exec/g_cur_fiber/g_thr_blocked around pumped thread slices (c) validate/repair thread ctx.r[15] zero PC -> entry and base/mem_size before running (d) bound pump iteration count never pump recursively; then re-run default+THRPUMP=1 check whether flag clears RDR appears boot advances toward render loop."),
    ("18.4264", "★★★★★ default boot stall pinpointed to one never-cleared global [0x816CC630]=2 set by app-init function FUN_811989C8 right after starting threads; new WAITLOOP probe on main wait loop 0x811E5EC2/EC6/ECE fiber 848468E0 shows main task object 0x84CF3E70 has [task+2]=0 forever (should advance to 6=done) while [0x816CC630]=2; loop only calls guest Fios step when [0x816CC630]&2==0 so it permanently takes pump branch 0x81207632 FiberGetSelf 0x812B1B70 -> GetThreadId 0x812B27B0 -> job dispatch 0x812067A0 -> DelayThread(30) and Fios state machine never stepped; new FLAG630 write watch found exactly one write v=2 blk=81198A6A fib=0 main context function FUN_811989C8; disassembly shows app-init routine memset [0x816CBC08+0xA24] store GetThreadId at [0x816CBC08+0xA20] load two sysmodules 0x812B1860 x2 sceAppUtilInit 0x812B1910 call 0x81198E2E create/start job threads 0x81206700 0x81206BA8 0x8120683C 0x8120690E then orrs r0,r2,#2 str [0x816CC630] and finally exit([sp]) via 0x812B22C0 but EXITLOG count is 0 proving function never reaches exit: it sets flag starts something never resumes/completes; two attempted fixes tested (a) Fios HLE signals guest Fios-worker event flags 0x60014000/0x60015000 on Fios open/read/opwait and wakes waiting guest threads (b) WaitEventFlag auto-sets those two flags when guest Fios worker threads wait; neither changed outcome still state=0 flag=2 RDR=0 FIOS=4 mount x2 + stripped-path + OPEN GFDPSP2PRESET.GSC 62,100 B GXM-REG=2 EXITLOG=0; default 30M remains stable exit=0 guest/HLE BADMEM=0 GXM=12 FSW=16; NEXT disassemble init helpers 0x81206700/0x81206BA8/0x8120683C/0x8120690E and identify unknown HLE stubs 0x812B2A80 x72k and 0x812B2920 learn how app-init context supposed to resume/complete after starting worker threads and what should clear [0x816CC630] then restore correct thread/fiber start semantics so init function returns flag clears Fios step runs task advances to state 6."),
    ("18.4263", "★★★★★ the two execution models progress through complementary halves of the boot sequence - neither completes the load->read flow; confirmed open-wrapper signature by disassembling head of FUN_81182C56 r6=r0 name string r7=r1 data pointer r8=r2 size allocates 0xA0 root dedupes global list [0x813B0184] length [list+0xA4]+strcmp then 0x81182D10 cbz r7 async - if r7!=0 stores [root+0x8C]=r7 [root+0x87]=1 [root+0x90]=r8 caller-provided payload otherwise [root+0x87]=0 strh #0,[root+4] type 0 calls FUN_81181A3C create 0xC8 file entry stores [root]=entry returns async pending; caller FUN_811C6C54 via table [0x81513DD4] passes r1=r2=r3=0 so async branch always taken payload must be delivered later but CHW write watch proved no writes ever reach entry +0x88/+0x94; mode comparison new evidence default cooperative run loads shader-preset file [FIOS] stripped data/ data/GFDPSP2PRESET.GSC -> GFDPSP2PRESET.GSC [FIOS] OPEN app0:/data/GFDPSP2PRESET.GSC -> fh=0x3001 size=62100 but never reaches reader-root creation RDR=0 RBUF=0 main loop stalls thread-pump/GetThreadId area last pc=812B27B0 blk=8120764C 30M blocks; host-thread run creates reader roots RDR=5 RBUF=5 CHILD=4 with empty payload then burns in 4GB swap pc=811DD4C8 but never performs Fios open FIOS=2 mount lines only; so default loads preset but stalls thread-join/pump host-thread runs threads but skips file-load stage; fixing divergence should marry load and read likely default block at 0x8120764C calls GetThreadId HLE 0x812B27B0 then loops is thread wait/join our model makes unsatisfiable while host-thread model satisfies join but orders file-load after main fiber passed load point; default 30M stable exit=0 guest/HLE BADMEM=0 GXM=12 FSW=16; NEXT disassemble 0x8120764C function around GetThreadId call identify wait/join semantics (main waiting for Gfd/Cri workers exit?) then implement wait correctly (default boot proceeds past join into reader path with loaded preset buffer) or reorder host-thread scheduling so Fios preset load runs before reader creation."),
    ("18.4262", "★★★★★ loader chain traced FUN_811C4556 -> FUN_811EEB98 is the GXM graphics init (it calls our new MapVertexUsse 0x812B17C0 / MapFragmentUsse 0x812B11C0 / CreateContext 0x812B11D0 stubs!) -> then creates the reader roots via thunk 0x811C6D98 -> 0x811EF362 (17x 0x811C651E); and the open+load function FUN_81182C56 data path is now clear: at 0x81182D10 cbz r7 it stores the caller-provided payload directly - if r7 (data pointer) != 0: [root+0x8C]=r7, [root+0x87]=1, [root+0x90]=r8 (size); else [root+0x87]=0 and the async branch runs: strh r0(=0),[root+4] (type 0), calls FUN_81181A3C(path,...) to create the 0xC8 file entry, stores [root]=entry, returns; so the reader root payload is supposed to come from already-loaded memory (r7/r8) or from the async file-entry fill; evidence (a) FUN_811C4556 (0x886-byte loader) call list: 0x811EEB98 (GXM init: MapVertexUsse 0x812B17C0, MapFragmentUsse 0x812B11C0, memset, CreateContext 0x812B11D0, then 0x811C53F0/0x811C5682 sub-loaders), 0x811C6D98 (reader-root thunk, called at 0x811C45EA), 0x811EF362 (17x 0x811C651E), 0x811C3E74, then heap allocs and 0x811CA432/0x811CAA02 state helpers; (b) open wrapper FUN_81182C56 invoked through virtual-FS table [0x81513DD4] from FUN_811C6C54 with r1=r2=r3=0 so it takes the async branch (type 0 + file entry) - payload never provided synchronously; (c) CHW write watch on root/child object region 0x84C0A480-0x84C0A600 recorded only 12 writes all v=0x84C09F40 from block 0x811EFFA6 (inside GXM loader) - no writes at all to child +0x88/+0x94 so async file-entry fill still never happens; default cooperative 30M re-verified exit=0 guest/HLE BADMEM=0 GXM=12 FSW=16 host-thread runs clean; NEXT disassemble head of FUN_81182C56 0x81182C56-0x81182D06 to find where r7/r8 come from (likely file-entry fields) and identify what block 0x811EFFA6 builds (GXM command/fence pointer array 0x84C09F40) then find async fill trigger (loader file-read completion) and wire it so [entry+0x88]/[entry+0x94] get populated."),
    ("18.4261", "★★★★ thread/semaphore/eventflag state at end of the host-thread run shows the GFD job queues are empty and the CRI oneshot threads completed normally - the file-entry payload fill is still never triggered; added an end-of-run THRDUMP (thread state + SEMA + EFLAGS dumps) and a 15M host-thread run produced 13 threads - the six Gfd workers 0x40011-0x40016 (entry 0x811E68C9) alive/ready; the CRI one-shot threads 0x40017-0x4001C (entry 0x8120767D) have alive=0 (completed normally: the entry is a one-shot callback invoker - r1=arg struct, r4=[r1+4] function pointer, r0=[r1+0xC] argument, blx r4, return 1 - not file workers); display thread 0x4001D000 (entry 0x811539F3) alive; Semaphores: gfdJobCountSema 0x50011000/0x50013000/0x50015000 = 0/0/0 (no jobs queued), gfdJobEmptySema 0x50012000/0x50014000/0x50016000 = 512/10240/8 (full), plus 0x50017000-0x50022000 = 1 each; Event flags: 0x60011000-0x60015000 = 0, 0x60016000 = 1 (CriCond); TOPBLK (block-dispatch histogram) shows main loop essentially 100% inside the byte-swap loop: blk 811DD4C8 x5,630,222, 811DD4D0 x5,629,964, 811DD4D8 x5,630,221 in a 15M-block run - confirming the pathological ~4GB swap dominates the entire run (count came from empty file-entry payload M709-M713); so neither Fios path nor GFD job path is being asked to read anything: payload fill triggered by a third mechanism whose condition is still unmet; default cooperative 30M re-verified exit=0 guest/HLE BADMEM=0 GXM=12 FSW=16; NEXT (a) find external callers of FUN_81181A3C the 0xC8 file-entry creator and trace what CRI open wrapper does right after creating the entry (does it call a read function pointer / post a job?) (b) add SEM2 probes on GFD job semaphores 0x50011000/13000/15000 counts and 0x50012000/14000/16000 empties to catch first job posting if it ever happens (c) if no job ever posted inspect the state machine condition that prevents the read request (likely the file-entry type/queue state we saw as 0)."),
    ("18.4260", "★★★★ full HLE-call census (92 unique stubs) shows no file open/read is ever called in the host-thread run - the CRI load pipeline is simply not reached yet; meanwhile 14 more GXM/audio stubs were identified and the GXM init/setup family was implemented; method raised the end-of-run HLECOUNT dump from top-40 to all stubs (92 unique in the 5M host-thread run, 23,775 calls) and cross-mapped every stub to its module/NID; result the only file/IO-related stub ever called is 0x812B19B0 sceFiosInitialize fios_init x1 - no Fios open/read, no sceIo*, no Libc stdio - so the CRI/GFD resource loader never even starts; the load request must be waiting on something else (consistent with the unfilled file-entry payload M709-M713); remaining default r0=0 set now well-defined GXM init/state helpers 0x812B11D0 CreateContext 0x812B1210/1240/1280/1310/1330/1380/1570/16E0/17D0 gxm state no-ops 0x812B14B0 GetNotificationRegion 0x812B1370 ProgramParameterGetResourceIndex x40 0x812B17C0 Map*UsseMemory plus SceNgs audio init stubs (~10, 1-6 calls each), SceRtcUser rtc_tick, SceTouch/SceNet/SceHttp/SceSsl/SceNp noops and a few Threadmgr/Libc helpers; implemented GXM ones with real semantics CreateContext allocates a 0x4000 fake context writes out pointer GetNotificationRegion returns stable 0x40-byte region ProgramParameterGetResourceIndex reads real resourceIndex@+0xC of GXP parameter (was returning 0 for all 40 calls) 0x812B17C0 aliases USSE-map stub state/no-op family returns success; verified host-thread 30M GXM-CTX params=A05FFD90 out=816CBE00 -> obj=84BC9530 x4 CreateContext GXM-REG 2 valid GXP headers magic 0x00505847 GXM-RT 2 GXM-CFP 1 GXM-CVP 1 GXM-FPS 2 exit=0 guest BADMEM=0 HLE-BADMEM=0; still GXM-BEGIN/GXM-PRESENT=0 and main loop still spins at pc=0x811DD4C8 byte swap; default cooperative 30M re-verified GXM=12 GXM-CTX=4 GXM-REG=2 GXM-BEGIN=0 FSW=16 guest/HLE BADMEM=0; also decoded tail of file-open function FUN_81181A3C it only fills the 0xC8 entry [entry]=r1 +4=r0 +0x90h=r2 +0xA4=name length +0xA8=r5 +0xAC=path via strcpy list links at +0xC0/+0xC4 and returns - it does not read any file data so payload +0x88/+0x94 must be filled by an asynchronous loader whose trigger we have not reached; NEXT capture CRI filer threads 0x40017/0x40018/0x40019 waiting on event 0x60014000/0x60015000 / CriCond 0x60016000 state in host-thread run and test signaling those events when a load request is queued (queue/global around 0x816CDAC8) if that wakes loader file-entry payload should fill and byte-swap spin should clear."),
    ("18.4259", "★★★★★ implemented the 8 HLE stubs the guest actually blocks on (WaitEventFlagCB + 7 SceGxm) and the shader pipeline now receives REAL GXP program headers (magic=0x00505847); method parsed the HLECOUNT top-40 dump of a host-thread run (91 unique stubs 25,007 calls) and cross-checked each stub against harness switch exactly 8 high-count stubs were falling into default r0=0 path 0x812B2930 WaitEventFlagCB SceLibKernel NID E737B1DF x64 0x812B1250 SceGxm no-op 12AAA7AF x11 0x812B1290 CreateRenderTarget 207AF96B x11 0x812B12D0 ShaderPatcherRegisterProgram 2B528462 x48 0x812B1350 CreateFragmentProgram 4ED2E49D x30 0x812B13A0 FindParameterBySemantic 633CAA54 x52 0x812B15C0 CreateVertexProgram B7BBA6D5 x18 0x812B11C0 MapFragmentUsseMemory 008402C6 x11; implemented all with real semantics ported from old runtime verified GXM behaviour WaitEventFlagCB aliases existing WaitEventFlag implementation RegisterProgram assigns ids g_prog_id_ctr stores id -> programHeader in g_prog_header_by_id writes id to out pointer CreateRenderTarget allocates 0x1000 fake object writes out pointer CreateFragmentProgram/CreateVertexProgram allocate 0x400/0x800 objects store registered header write object to correct stack out-slot sp+8/sp+4 FindParameterBySemantic parses real GXP header layout parameter_count@+0x24 params base prog+0x28+[prog+0x28] 16-byte entries semantic@+6 index@+7 MapFragmentUsseMemory writes 0 offset returns 0 GetProgramFromId returns registered real header instead of blind fake; VERIFIED host-thread 30M emits GXM-REG hdr=81539944 magic=00505847 id=1 hdr=8153985C magic=00505847 id=2 hdr=8153D318 magic=00505847 id=3 valid GXP shader programs plus 2x GXM-RT CreateRenderTarget 1x GXM-CFP CreateFragmentProgram 1x GXM-CVP CreateVertexProgram 3x GXM-FPS FindParameterBySemantic default config registers 2 programs; host-thread 30M exit=0 guest BADMEM=0 default 30M exit=0 guest BADMEM=0 HLE-BADMEM=0 GXM=12 FSW=16; still GXM-BEGIN/GXM-PRESENT=0 render loop not reached yet byte-swap spin pc=0x811DD4C8 from unfilled CRI file-entry payload M709-M713 remains current blocker; NEXT keep real-GXP registry as basis for draw path continue unblocking resource payload child file-entry +0x88/+0x94 so boot proceeds past byte-swap as new GXM stubs appear in HLECOUNT implement them on top of this registry render-target views samplers texture upload draw/commit."),
    ("18.4258", "★★★★ the child stream object 0x84C0A520 is a real HLE allocation 0xC8 bytes via SceLibc calloc (stub 0x812B23E0 NID 0xE7EC3D0B) through the guest libc wrapper 0x811E6A28 (only call site 0x811DA54E inside thunk 0x811DA54C) not the guest heap allocator; evidence extended CHILD probe now looks up child pointer in g_arec HLE-allocation records child=84C0A520 ctype=0 c88=0 c8c=0 c94=0 ca0=0 asz=000000C8 astub=812B23E0 alr=811E6A2E i.e. child allocated through SceLibc calloc stub size 0xC8 return address 0x811E6A2E guest libc wrapper 0x811E6A28 push blx 0x812B23E0 pop; scan of whole image finds exactly one call site of that wrapper 0x811DA54E inside 8-byte thunk 0x811DA54C so creator reaches calloc through that thunk; guest heap-allocator probe GALLOC at 0x811DA55C 124 calls in 5M shows only small objects 0x1C etc. from 81207748 plus 0x0C/0x14 from 81207930/811A7DA0/811C17E8 the 0xC8 child never goes through it confirming calloc path; block-dispatch probes at thunk address do not fire AOT block boundaries so creator must be captured by HLE allocation record PC ring instead; default cooperative config stable 30M exit=0 BADMEM=0 GXM=12 FSW=16 host-thread 5M clean exit=0 BADMEM=0; NEXT in hle_malloc_ret add targeted dump when p==0x84C0A520 and generally for calloc requests of size 0xC8 print g_pc_ring last 32 PCs g_cur_block g_cur_fiber/g_cur_thr ring reveals guest creator function then disassemble it find where [child+0x88] size and [child+0x94] buffer supposed written and why load never happens candidate async CRI read completion/callback or file open HLE serves as empty."),
    ("18.4257", "★★★★ the type-3 open state machine is now fully decoded the root reader payload is copied from a child stream object ([root+0]=child payload [child+0x94] size [child+0x88]) and that child is completely uninitialised (type=0 all data fields 0); (1) FUN_811830C8 (table [0x81513DE4] called from FUN_811C6C54 right after open) is a spin-wait until [obj+4]==3 ldrsh r0,[r4,#4] cmp #3 bne movw r0,#0x7530 bl DelayThread loop sleep 30000us the synchronous open completed barrier (2) FUN_811830E2 (table [0x81513DF0]) is the pump/state machine over global root list [0x813B0184] for a root with type 0 whose child r7=[root] has type 0xC if [root+0x87]==0 it runs zero-copy path [root+0x8C]=[child+0x94] [root+0x90]=[child+0x88] [root+6]=0 else memcpy [child+0x94] into [root+0x8C] then sets [root+4]=3 type; actual payload pointer/size come from child stream object fields +0x94 buffer +0x88 size (3) new CHILD dump at creator return every root object carries same child pointer 0x84C0A520 and that child entirely empty ctype=0 c88=0 c8c=0 c94=0 ca0=0 later read wrapper sees roots type=3 but ptr/size=0 i.e. pump zero-copy path ran with child data fields still zero open succeeded but empty (4) real missing link is child stream data load who writes [child+0x88] size and [child+0x94] buffer that is CRI/GFD async file read path whose completion/callback still not delivered (previous evidence 4 GB swap empty readers); default cooperative config stable 30M exit=0 BADMEM=0 GXM=12 FSW=16 libc fixes M711 keep host-thread 5M clean exit=0 BADMEM=0; NEXT probe pump paths 0x81183184 zero-copy and 0x81183142 memcpy capture child state at type becomes 3 find who allocates/initialises child 0x84C0A520 search writers [root+0]/[child+0x94]/[child+0x88] trace async read completion should fill child likely Fios op completion/event flag never signalled by HLE."),
    ("18.4256", "★★★★ SceLibc gap found and partially filled 21 missing SceLibc functions including strcmp memcmp memmove strncpy strncmp snprintf errno_loc and a creation-time object dump shows reader object born empty (type=0 payload=0) so a later open/retry step sets type=3 but still not the payload; (1) audited all SceLibc imports in 0x812B2200..0x812B2700 against harness switch 14 present / 21 missing missing list includes 0x812B2200 strcmp NID 1B58FA3B 0x812B2290 memcmp 7747F6D7 0x812B2350 memmove AF5C218D 0x812B2310 strncpy 9F87712D 0x812B23B0 strncmp E4299DCB 0x812B2320 snprintf A1BFF606 0x812B2300 errno_loc 9E248B76 0x812B2220 __cxa_atexit 0x812B2230 malloc_usable_size 0x812B2380 clock 0x812B2390 time 0x812B2400 localtime plus vfprintf/printf_stub/sscanf/qsort/strtoull helpers; crucially strcmp defaulted to 0 strings equal corrupting guest string comparisons on CRI loader path; implemented real versions strcmp/memcmp/memmove/strncpy/strncmp + basic register/stack-vararg guest_format for snprintf + errno_loc/malloc_usable_size/cxa_atexit/clock/time/localtime (2) new CREATED2 dump at creator return block 0x811C6C72 shows reader object as delivered +00=84C0A520 shared global pointer +9C=previous-object linked list everything else 0 notably +04=0 type and +8C=0 +90=0 payload pointer/size; yet later RDR read shows type=3 so some step between creation and read sets type=3 without populating payload i.e. open succeeded but empty or partially-initialised state (3) libc fixes compile and run host-thread 5M exit=0 BADMEM=0 readers still ptr=0 size=0; default cooperative re-verified 30M exit=0 BADMEM=0 GXM=12 FSW=16; NEXT find code writes [obj+4]=3 between creation and read probe blocks after 0x811C6C74 in FUN_811C6C54 or scan for writers offset +4 on type-3 open state machine check whether guest open/retry consumes empty-handle response OPEN-MISS policy also re-check vita.cpk index completeness only 531 entries parsed from 2.17 GB CPK suspiciously low so miss may begin at TOC parsing."),
    ("18.4255", "★★★★ reader objects exist with type=3 but their data fields [obj+0x8C]/[obj+0x90] are 0 - the CRI/GFD virtual-FS table and creator chain are now mapped and a full sceIo* HLE layer was added (but unused by this path); (1) new RDR probe at read wrapper 0x8118308B (guest func installed in [0x81513DE0] called from 0x811E5C98) shows all 5 objects with type=3 (type field [obj+4] is 3 so branch correct) but ptr=[obj+0x8C]=0 size=[obj+0x90]=0 i.e. file/memory-stream payload fields never populated (earlier RBUF empty-ring is consequence not cause) (2) virtual-FS table resolved [0x81513DD4]=0x81182C56 create/open [0x81513DD8]=0x8118307B is-type-3 [0x81513DDC]=0x81182F6B close/refcount [0x81513DE0]=0x8118308B read returns [obj+0x8C] writes size [obj+0x90] [0x81513DE4]=0x811830C9 [0x81513DE8]=0x81182F1D [0x81513DF0]=0x8118321D; creator 0x81182C56 allocates 0xA0-byte object links list and only uses SceLibc primitives 0x81182D48 blx 0x812B22D0 strcpy 0x81182D4E/0x81182D84 blx 0x812B22E0 strlen 0x81182DCE blx 0x812B2200 0x81182E9A blx 0x812B2270 memcpy plus guest helpers 0x8118192C/0x81181D90/0x81181A3C so data fields must be filled either by one of those Libc stubs whose return value we return as 0 candidate 0x812B2200 = NID 0x1B58FA3B currently unhandled default 0 or by guest helper chain (3) added complete sceIo* HLE layer SceIofilemgr 0x812B2970 open 0x812B29B0 read 0x812B2990 lseek32 0x812B29A0 close 0x812B2980 dclose backed by cpk_read_any_impl + fd map compiles stable but CRI path never calls it IO count=0 so payload loss elsewhere; default cooperative config stable after changes 30M exit=0 BADMEM=0 GXM=12 FSW=16 host-thread 5M exit=0 BADMEM=0 readers still ptr=0 size=0; NEXT dump 0xA0-byte creator object right after creation at 0x811E5C72 and again at read wrapper see which fields populated when implement/repair 0x812B2200 NID 0x1B58FA3B if memmove/memcpy-class whose return creator uses then trace guest helper chain 0x8118192C/0x81181D90/0x81181A3C find where payload pointer/size should come from."),
    ("18.4254", "★★★★★ empty ring-buffer reader traced to a CPK/file record loader whose indirect calls through guest function-pointer globals 0x81513DD4/DD8/DE0/DE4/DE8 return 0; (1) decoded reader factory FUN_811DEAB4(type=r0 u16 flags=r1 u16 param=r2) allocates 0x24-byte object memsets for type=3 copies 0xC bytes from param into [obj+0x18] ring pos/limit/buffer then sets [obj+0x10]=type [obj+0x12]=flags when flags&1 it immediately reads 0x10 bytes from empty reader and endian-swaps them empty ring read returns -1 unchecked count -> 4 GB swap M707/M708 (2) new RFACT probe 5M host-thread all 5 reader creations come from lr=811C6C90 guest FUN_811C6C54 with type=0003 flags=0001 param={0,0,0} all-zero stack struct built as bl 0x811E5C66 movs r0,#0 str r0,[sp] add r1,sp,#4 bl 0x811E5C98 str r0,[sp,#8] then bl 0x811DEAB4 (3) wrappers 0x811E5C66/0x811E5C98 are indirect calls through guest globals [0x81513DD4]/[0x81513DD8]/[0x81513DE0]/[0x81513DE4]/[0x81513DE8] ldr r4,[0x81513DD4] blx r4 populated by init code around 0x811E5C0A/0x811E5BEA with stub addresses i.e. import/function-pointer table; in this run indirect call returns 0 writes nothing [sp+4] stays 0 so 0xC-byte ring params all zero reader born empty factory initial read/byteswap enters 4 GB loop (4) missing link is whichever HLE stub installed at [0x81513DE0] must be a read/lookup returning actual record data; default cooperative config stable 30M exit=0 BADMEM=0 GXM=12 FSW=16; NEXT log which stub VA written to 0x81513DD4..DF0 at init probe stores at 0x811E5C0A/init or read globals at first RFACT call map stub to NID via docs/eboot_imports_with_nid.json fix that HLE function to produce real record data likely Fios/CPK read or memblock/stream getter so type-3 readers created with non-empty ring."),
    ("18.4253", "★★★★ the 4 GB byte-swap loop is caused by empty type-3 ring-buffer readers whose FUN_811DE912 read returns -1 (0xFFFFFFFF) and the caller uses it as a word count; follow-up analysis of M707 FUN_811DE912(reader,dst,0x10) is a ring/stream read entry checks [reader+0x12]&1 valid -> if clear return -1 type [reader+0x10] selects path type 3 (and 0/2) use ring pointers [reader+0x18] read pos [reader+0x1C] limit [reader+0x20] buffer when ring empty pos==limit==0 type-3 path returns -1 and caller at 0x811DEB44 passes that return unchecked into endian-swap adds r2,r0 -> 0x811DD4BC producing 0x3FFFFFFF-word ~4 GB loop; new RBUF probe 5M host-thread run caught 5 such reader objects obj=84C0A5F0/84F2BD20/8831CE20/8B70DF20/8C3BF320 all f10=0003 type 3 f12=0001 flag valid f18=0 f1c=0 f20=0 empty ring and ret=FFFFFFFF; readers exist and marked valid but ring buffers never filled data-loading/fill path missing or failing; FUN_811DEAB4 caller function uses these readers has 26 call sites 8119C204 8119C252 8119C2CC 8119C694 8119C70A 811AB252 811AB2D8 811ABBC2 811B7CD8 811B7D72 likely GFD/GSC resource decode path; default cooperative config stable 30M exit=0 BADMEM=0 GXM=12 FSW=16; NEXT symbolize FUN_811DEAB4 and its 26 callers identify subsystem GFD resource/file stream find object creation site 5 objects same layout which fill/read function should set [obj+0x18]/[obj+0x1C] then implement/repair HLE load-fill path so readers contain data and endian conversion proceeds correctly."),
    ("18.4252", "★★★★★ the host-thread run is no longer crashing but it is spinning in a 4 GB byte-swap loop - root cause: a guest helper returned 0 and the caller passed count-1 = 0xFFFFFFFF to the endian swap; long-run evidence host-thread 300M blocks exit=0 BADMEM=0 still never reaches GXM-BEGIN every FRAMEDUMP sample at pc=811DD4C8 blk=811DD4E0 the endian-swap loop 0x811DD4BC ldr r1,[r0] rev/bfi str r3,[r0],#4 subs r2,#1 bne; new BSWAP probe shows first call with r0=r1=84C0A5F0 r2=FFFFFFFF lr=811DEB4E count 0xFFFFFFFF -> lsrs r2,r2,#2 = 0x3FFFFFFF words = ~4 GB of swapping effectively infinite loop and reads/writes far past intended buffer; disassembly caller 811DEB44 adds r2,r0,#0 811DEB46 adds r0,r4,#0 811DEB48 adds r1,r4,#0 811DEB4A bl 0x811DD4BC where r0 = FUN_811DE912(r4,r4,0x10) so FUN_811DE912 returned 0 empty/zero structure in r4 and caller passes raw return value 0 -> underflows to 0xFFFFFFFF as word count without check; everything else now stable 300M host-thread blocks 111 memblocks no BADMEM clean exit 0; default cooperative run stable 30M exit=0 BADMEM=0 GXM=12 FSW=16; NEXT disassemble FUN_811DE912 to see what it counts in r4 structure candidate list/table count or size field probe r4 structure bytes at 0x811DEB44 why empty then trace producer of that structure caller chain of 0x811DEBxx find which resource/HLE path should have filled it likely fake GXM object or load returning empty."),
    ("18.4251", "★★★★★ the OOM crash is fixed - host-thread 30M run is now clean exit=0 BADMEM=0 111 memblocks; added a 96 MB extra guest memory window VA 0xA2000000-0xA8000000 mapped to free host tail image+0x2A000000..0x30000000 in BOTH harness GP() and AOT batch prelude P() (one extra branch in _gen_split.py) and hle_malloc gained a BIG2 fallback arena g_big2_ptr=0xA2000000..0xA8000000; regenerated all 26 batches compiled 26/26 ok in 422.5s plus relink; result previously failing 15 MB memblock now allocated BIG2 n=00F00100 -> A2000000 MEMA uid=0x16B no longer base 0 guest now creates 111 memblocks (was 107 last one OOM) and host-thread run completes 30,000,000 blocks with exit=0 BADMEM=0 (previously always died at exactly 7,863,834 blocks with BADMEM va=8); also added clean shutdown for concurrency model g_shutdown flag + atexit join of all guest host threads wait/lock poll loops honour shutdown because earlier run ended with 0xC0000005 during teardown with detached threads after fix exit clean 0; still no rendering gxm(b/e/p)=0/0/0 framectr=0 last FRAMEDUMP pc=811DD4C8 blk=811DD4E0 fib=848484E0 next blocker downstream GXM/display object initialisation / BeginScene routing; default cooperative config re-verified 30M exit=0 BADMEM=0 GXM=12 FSW=16; NEXT on top of now-clean host-thread run chase next visible milestone instrument GXM call path BeginScene/EndScene/DisplayQueueAddEntry never called and guest graphics task state machine at 0x811DD4xx find condition preventing render loop start."),
    ("18.4250", "★★★★★ root cause of the deterministic crash found: guest memory arena exhaustion OOM in our HLE - the 15 MB memblock request uid=0x16B size=0x00F00000 returns base 0 which becomes the null descriptor; evidence MEMA AllocMemBlock uid=0000016B size=00F00000 addr=00000000 and MEMB GetMemBlockInfo uid=0000016B -> base=00000000 size=00F00000 info=8460F150 our hle_malloc returned 0 for the 15 MB request so FUN_81207734 stored base=0 into descriptor [desc+0]; later guest calls free-like 0x811C0D74(NULL,0xF00000) -> [r0+8] -> BADMEM va=8 blk=0x811C0DA8; total guest memblock demand measured 107 allocations summing 458.5 MB (largest 58 MB, 50 MB x3, 15 MB x4, 8 MB...) while mapped guest-memory capacity only ~462 MB total (big arena 320 MB + heapA 96 MB + heaps 8/14/10/8/6 MB) minus other HLE allocations/fragmentation so last 15 MB request fails; failing descriptor 0x8460F150 is guest heap memory consistent with M704; first fix attempt added 17 MB reserve arena at VA 0x81700000-0x82800000 unused image window already mapped by both GP and batch P for LARGE allocations only; reserve consumed by four earlier large allocations 4/8/3.3/1.2 MB and 15 MB request still failed capacity short by roughly 15-30 MB; default cooperative run re-verified stable 30M exit=0 BADMEM=0 GXM=12 FSW=16; NEXT add a new 96 MB VA window 0xA2000000-0xA8000000 mapped to free host tail image+0x2A000000..+0x30000000 requires one extra branch in batch prelude P and harness GP plus batch regeneration ~7 min then total capacity ~558 MB > 458 MB demand 0x16B memblock should allocate crash point should move past 7,863,834."),
    ("18.4249", "★★★★ the null descriptor is guest-managed memory, not a hle_malloc object - attribution probes rule out our allocator and memblock bases; added per-allocation attribution hle_malloc now records {ptr,size,stub,lr} for every heap-A allocation 0x84600000..0x8C600000 prints AREC-TARGET for 0x8460F000-0x84610000 and harness_badmem dumps that window; result no AREC-TARGET lines no heap-A allocations in 0x8460F000-0x84610000 and no memblock base anywhere near 0x8460F150 (107 MEMA bases start at 0x84A625C0 / 0x8C9008D0); therefore failing descriptor 0x8460F150 comes from guest-managed memory it lies inside the guest heap window our address space maps for the guest (same region guest own 0x811DA55C heap allocator uses) so its [0]==0 is genuine guest state the resource/data pointer was never filled rather than an uninitialised HLE object as M703 hypothesised; refines target either guest-side load that should fill [0] returned empty (again pointing to I/O/loader semantics gap but now within guest-managed structures) or a guest initialisation branch was skipped because of a prior HLE return value; default cooperative config stable 30M exit=0 BADMEM=0 GXM=12 FSW=16; NEXT disassemble more of 0x81207734 descriptor factory and 0x811DA55C guest heap alloc to see what fills [desc+0] and under which condition instrument guest heap allocations near 0x8460F150 indirectly by watching write to [desc+0] find store site via static analysis of 0x81207734 and its helpers then compare with old runtime successful boot where this path completed."),
    ("18.4248", "★★★★★ 64-bit file seek fix vita.cpk NOW MOUNTS files=531 but the deterministic host-thread crash is unchanged so its null descriptor is NOT a missing vita.cpk resource; two results (1) root-caused mount failure CpkReader used std::fseek(fp,long(off)) and on Windows long is 32-bit so any offset above 2^31 silently failed; vita.cpk is 2,168,403,092 bytes; added cpk_seek using _fseeki64 POSIX fseeko and replaced both seek sites; verified FIOS mounted vita.cpk files=531 data.cpk still 10,555 and file app0:/data/GFDPSP2PRESET.GSC 62,100 B still opens correctly (2) host-thread crash still stops at exactly total=7,863,834 BADMEM va=0x00000008 blk=0x811C0DA8 2 occurrences so M702 hypothesis missing resources from un-mounted vita.cpk not the cause of this crash; further analysis failing descriptor guest FUN_81207924 receives descriptor from 0x81207734 descriptor address seen at failure 0x8460F150 inside hle_malloc heap-A arena its [0] field is 0 while [+8] is a size i.e. guest reading a fake object our HLE allocated from heapA whose data-pointer field was never filled; guest then calls free-like 0x811C0D74(NULL,size) NULL+8 dereference; default cooperative config re-verified after CPK change 30M exit=0 BADMEM=0 GXM=12 FSW=16; NEXT instrument hle_malloc record size caller lr active stub for every allocation in 0x8460F000-0x84610000 range attribute object 0x8460F150 to exact HLE call then initialise correct data pointer/size fields for that fake object candidate GXM program/parameter fake or resource-loader stub returning hle_malloc(0x200) and re-run host-thread 30M crash point should move past 7,863,834."),
    ("18.4247", "★★★★ new high-value lead for the deterministic crash: vita.cpk EXISTS on disk 2,168,403,092 bytes with a valid CPK header but our CpkReader fails to mount it - so the game is running with missing resources; discovery chain (a) crash always at total=7,863,834 on free path (b) FREE2 probes show free-like function 0x811C0D74 called with NULL block pointer that comes from a descriptor built by guest FUN_81207924 it allocates 0xc bytes bl 0x811DA55C calls 0x81207734 returns descriptor then ldr r0,[desc] data pointer and ldr r1,[desc,#8] size and calls 0x811C0D74(r0,r1); on failing iteration [desc]==0 so free path dereferences NULL+8 BADMEM guest va=0x00000008 block=0x811C0DA8 (c) real question why that data pointer is NULL i.e. resource loading returned empty handle/zero pointer (d) our own fios log says FIOS WARN vita.cpk not mounted even though C:/dev/p5d_rom/data/vita.cpk exists size 2,168,403,092 bytes and valid CRI CPK header 43 50 4B 20 FF FF FF FF ... 40 55 54 46 CPK @UTF while data.cpk 1,913,750,232 bytes header CPK ff 00 00 00 50 03 mounts fine with 10,555 entries; suspect reader header/TOC parsing does not handle vita.cpk variant version bytes FF FF FF FF maybe UTF table offsets or >2GB file offsets so parse_header/parse_toc fail and open returns false; default cooperative run stable 30M exit=0 BADMEM=0 GXM=12 FSW=16; NEXT add temporary debug to CpkReader::parse_header/parse_toc print fields toc offset/size entry count and run quick 2M harness to see exactly where vita.cpk parsing fails then fix support observed header variant / 2GB+ offsets and re-run host-thread 30M crash point should move past 7,863,834."),
    ("18.4246", "★★★★ the host-thread crash is deterministic and its last step is a free-like call with a null block pointer not an allocation failure; the run always stops at exactly total=7,863,834 blocks; new FREE2 probes at guest free path 0x81207956 -> 0x811C0D74 show guest calling free-like function with valid block pointers first r0=9BF69010/850DC520/9EECEB10/884CD620 all inside our big arena 0x8C600000..0xA0000000 i.e. buffers we allocated for guest memory blocks and then with r0=00000000 while r5=8460EF50 a guest object i.e. a field of that guest structure is NULL and guest calls free path with it anyway; FUN_811C0D74 then movs r2,#0 str r0,[r0,#8] BADMEM guest va=00000008 block=0x811C0DA8; earlier allocation-path probes 0x811DA024/0x811DA028 never fire on failing path so defect is which HLE-provided pointer guest stored into that structure field not the guest allocator itself; candidates a resource/loader getter that returned 0 e.g. memblock base for one uid or a GXM/CPK resource pointer or failed file load whose length/pointer stayed 0; default cooperative config stable 30M exit=0 BADMEM=0 GXM=12 FSW=16; NEXT disassemble 0x81207956 to identify structure/offset that yields NULL trace which HLE call writes that field add targeted probe on store site and on GetMemBlockBase/loader getters returning 0 then fix that HLE path and re-run host-thread 30M crash point should move past 7,863,834."),
    ("18.4245", "★★★★ main-thread LwMutex now real in host-thread mode; guest progress jumped to 7,863,834 blocks (was ~1.89M) with 6 guest threads exiting normally - same guest-null-allocator crash remains at the end; changes sceKernelLockLwMutex/UnlockLwMutex now take real per-work owner/count lock for every thread in host-thread mode including main thread me = tl_ht_tid ? tl_ht_tid : 0x40010000 because otherwise main thread and host threads race on guest heap protected only by guest LwMutex wrappers; new ALLOC2 probes at guest allocator call/entry 0x811DA024/0x811DA534 143 allocation requests observed with plausible arguments sizes 0x2C 0x10027 0x4000 0x74 lr 811D9DCC/811D9E50/811E6066/811E6074/81198F26 guest heap really being used; RESULT host-thread run total=7,863,834 blocks executed HT-EXIT=6 guest threads exiting normally VBLANK=8 GXM=12; remaining failure same guest-side pattern BADMEM guest va=0x00000008 block=0x811C0DA8 2 occurrences now in fiber context cur=848484E0 in_fex=1 sp=A0D7FE68 guest allocator still eventually returns null block caller dereferences fe_ring 81207352/Unlock -> 811C0D74 -> 811C0D86 -> 811C0DA8 r0=0; default cooperative config unchanged 30M exit=0 BADMEM=0 GXM=12 FSW=16; NEXT trace failing allocation request after ~7.8M blocks which allocator size/state verify guest heap arena size vs memblock HLE sizes GetMemBlockBase returns bases allocated with hle_malloc check requested vs granted sizes whether guest heap can grow inspect guest allocator FUN_811DA534 failure branch directly."),
    ("18.4244", "★★★★ last host-thread crash traced to a guest-side allocator returning NULL (not an HLE mapping bug); memblock HLE verified correct; harness_badmem now prints faulting thread id active HLE stub and its own PC chain which shows remaining BADMEM va=0x00000008 blk=0x811C0DA8 happens on main thread tid=0 with stub=812B28A0 UnlockLwMutex previously active; g_pc_ring chain 811D9FAA/811D9FAE/811D9FB0/811D9FBE loop -> 811D9FE2 -> 811D9FCA/94/9C -> 811DA008 -> 811DA03A unlock wrapper 81207352 -> 811DA040 -> 811DA08E -> 0x811C0DA8 allocator FUN_811C0D74 with r0=0; disassembly FUN_811D9F4A shows allocates via guest bl 0x811DA534 when returned block pointer sl is 0 it unlocks and returns r0=r4 possibly null block head caller then enters allocator block 0x811C0DA8 first instruction movs r2,#0 str r0,[r0,#8] guest own allocation failed and guest dereferences null result; also verified memory-block HLE correct MEMA 107 sceKernelAllocMemBlock NID B9D5EBDE all mapped MEMB 107 sceKernelGetMemBlockBase NID B8EF5818 all hits uid->base correct sceKernelFreeMemBlock 0x812B29D0 NID A91E15EE; remaining failure guest allocator behavior under host-thread model concurrency or genuine arena exhaustion not stub mis-map; default cooperative config stable 30M exit=0 BADMEM=0 GXM=12 FSW=16; NEXT instrument guest allocator FUN_811DA534 request size arena/free-list pointers and caller fields [fp+8]/[fp+0xc]/[fp+0x10] why request fails compare against default cooperative run check whether host-thread concurrency corrupts guest allocator state despite LwMutex wrappers main thread tid=0 also needs correct LwMutex behavior."),
    ("18.4243", "★★★★★ SceDisplay NID mapping was wrong - fixing it eliminated the 17137-BADMEM crash loop 8787 -> 2 and the guest vblank thread now works; verified against real import table 0x812B1810 = NID 0x05F27764 sceDisplayWaitVblankStartMultiCB NOT GetFrameBuf 0x812B1820 = NID 0x7D9864A8 sceDisplayWaitSetFrameBufMulti NOT SetFrameBuf real SetFrameBuf is 0x812B1800 = NID 0x7A410B64 SceDisplayUser and 0x812B2410 = NID 0xFBA69BC2 strncat was missing; root cause long crash loop guest graphics code 0x811539F2 calls sceDisplayWaitVblankStartMultiCB(2) in a loop our mis-mapped HLE treated that argument as frame-buffer pointer and did GP(r0=2) HLE-BADMEM va=00000002 repeated thousands times; fix new 0x812B1800 SetFrameBuf records addr/pitch 0x812B1810 vblank wait increments vblank counter host-thread path sleeps count*16ms count clamped 1..4 0x812B1820 WaitSetFrameBufMulti 1ms sleep and a real strncat HLE; RESULT host-thread run BADMEM dropped 8787 to 2 VBLANK count=2 fires regularly from guest graphics thread tid 0x4001D000 GXM=12 HT-RUN=13 SIG2=10; remaining single crash BADMEM guest va=0x00000008 block=0x811C0DA8 allocator-family block ring 811D9FAA 811D9FAE next target; default cooperative config unchanged 30M exit=0 BADMEM=0 GXM=12 FSW=16; LESSON every HLE stub NID must be verified against real import table docs/eboot_imports_with_nid.json not just stub-address comments a single wrong display-stub mapping produced entire crash loop and masked all deeper progress."),
    ("18.4242", "★★★★ thread-local PC ring pinpoints the bad-pointer chain: a worker graphics thread reaches the app-state machine and calls sceDisplayGetFrameBuf with an invalid buffer pointer; new diagnostic HLE-BADMEM prints host thread last-24-pc ring tl_pc_ring recorded inside guest_thread_run so bad access attributed exactly; host-thread run shows chain tlring 811539F2 811539F4 81236D22 8127B7 -> blk=8122C6DC stub=812B1810 i.e. guest section polygon FUN_811539E6 -> kernel/sequences/app-state machine FUN_81236D22/FUN_8127B7AC -> FUN_8122C6B6 -> HLE 0x812B1810 sceDisplayGetFrameBuf with r0=2 invalid buffer pointer; same pattern repeats via 81279238 stub=812B2410 and blk=8122C6F6/8122C718 stub=812B1810; confirms M696 hypothesis at deeper level guest graphics/display state machine now running on worker thread reads uninitialised fake GXM/display structure field producing pointer 2; remaining gap not concurrency model working 13 host threads real semaphores but structural fidelity of GXM/display objects HLE hands to guest; default config stable 30M exit=0 BADMEM=0 GXM=12 FSW=16; NEXT probe registers at 0x8122C6B6/0x8122C718 display-call block to identify which structure field yields 2 identify struct passed through polygon FUN_811539E6 initialise fake GXM objects SceGxmProgram/Parameter/display buffers with valid magic/sizes/offsets per real layouts."),
    ("18.4241", "★★★★ host-thread run now reaches deep guest code - the next bottleneck class is structurally invalid fake GXM objects not the thread model; added diagnostics HLE-BADMEM now prints active HLE stub and host-thread tid and hle_malloc is mutex-protected for multi-thread use 18.4241; host-thread run evidence GXM=12 HT-RUN=13 SIG2=10; first bad accesses HLE-BADMEM va=00000002 blk=8122C6F6 stub=812B1810 sceDisplayGetFrameBuf blk=811539F0 stub=812B2410 blk=81279258 stub=812B1810 guest workers now run deep GXM/display code and pass pointer value 2 as buffer/object pointer; expected next frontier our HLE returns fake non-null pointers e.g. sceGxmShaderPatcherGetProgramFromId -> hle_malloc(0x200) uninitialised sceGxmProgramFindParameterByName -> fake param and guest code dereferences struct fields to compute further pointers uninitialised/fake layouts produce garbage like 2; thread model itself proven to run 13 concurrent guest threads and deliver real semaphore signals; default config stable 30M exit=0 BADMEM=0 GXM=12 FSW=16; NEXT (1) identify guest 0x811539F0 / 0x81279258 callers to see which struct field yields 2 (2) make fake GXM objects structurally valid per SceGxmProgram/SceGxmProgramParameter/display struct layouts initialise magic/fields write real sizes/offsets expected by guest GSC loader (3) keep host-thread mode as primary experimental path."),
    ("18.4240", "★★★★★ host-thread model debugged - critical next-pc bug fixed; 13 guest threads now really run, SIG2 signals appear for the first time; root cause of previous thread-entry crash guest_thread_run executed pc=s->r[15] after each block instead of following the block returned next-pc nx; AOT block for Gfd thread wrapper 0x811E68C8 pushes its frame and returns its own pc so every host thread re-executed 0x811E68C8 forever stack shrinking by 0x48 per iteration 84664480->84664438; fixed to pc=nx 18.4240; evidence after fix HTBLK trace shows correct sequence in every worker 811E68C8 -> 811E68D8 -> 811E68EE -> 811E68F2 -> 812B27A0 and WaitSema call carries real semaphore object and args r0=50011000 r1=1 sp=84664438 lr=811E68FC exactly guest design; HT-RUN count rose to 13 GXM=12 preserved SIG2 count=10 SignalSema was ZERO in every cooperative run main path finally signals semaphores; new crash HLE-BADMEM hle access va=00000002 blk=8122C718 ring 8118651C repeated 17137 bad accesses guest worker dereferences near-null pointer most likely because per-thread TLS page at r9 is zeroed instead of initialised from main thread TLS template or due to unhandled thread-exit state; default config untouched 30M exit=0 BADMEM=0 GXM=12 FSW=16; NEXT (1) inspect guest 0x8122C718 and caller ring 0x8118651C to identify which per-thread structure is null (2) initialise each thread TLS r9 as COPY of main thread TLS page instead of zeros Vita kernel does this from main thread TLS template (3) handle guest thread exit ExitThread/pc sentinel and remove dead threads from scheduler maps."),
    ("18.4239", "★★★★ host-thread concurrency model MVP implemented per p5r-android architecture - scaffolding works and default config stays stable, thread entry semantics still need debugging; new opt-in P5D_HOSTTHREADS=1 turns every guest thread created via sceKernelCreateThread/sceKernelStartThread into a real host std::thread with its own RecState plus base/mem_size copied so AOT memory ops work and TLS page; sceKernelWaitSema/sceKernelWaitEventFlag really block 200us poll loop no cooperative pump sceKernelDelayThread sleeps and sceKernelLockLwMutex/UnlockLwMutex use a real per-work owner/count map g_lwm_real so guest critical sections are mutually exclusive; hle_thr_pump disabled in this mode; evidence first run HT-START/HT-RUN showed 7 guest host threads starting and running tids 0x40011xxx..0x40017xxx entry 0x811E68C8 versus 0 in old single-threaded model; two issues (a) first crash BADMEM va=0x8466447C memsize=0 block=0x811E68C8 because per-thread RecState.base/mem_size were zero fixed by copying from creator context (b) after fix run starts 2 threads then hits BADMEM guest va=0xFFFFFFF8 block=0x811E68C8 Gfd thread-start wrapper 0x811E68C8 with LR sentinel 0xFFFFFFF0 per-thread initial context/args need to match what wrapper expects; default config untouched re-verified 30M exit=0 BADMEM=0 GXM=12 FSW=16; NEXT instrument first 20 blocks of a host thread and exact register state at entry r0=arglen r1=argp r9 TLS sp compare old runtime n_start_thread context construction regs[13]=stacktop regs[14]=EXIT_SENTINEL regs[15]=entry|1 regs[0]=arglen regs[1]=eff_argp add sentinel guards in host-thread loop then re-test; first real step of architecture pivot toward thread-per-guest-thread."),
    ("18.4238", "★★★★ real CPK file semantics verified - the guest now opens actual game data GFDPSP2PRESET.GSC 62100 B and the P5D_LOADCLEAR=1 forced path crashes only at the null shader-patcher global; evidence FIOS mounted data.cpk files=10555 real C:/dev/p5d_rom/data/data.cpk FIOS WARN vita.cpk not mounted that dump absent locally FIOS OPEN app0:/data/GFDPSP2PRESET.GSC -> fh=0x3001 size=62100 and FIOS stripped data/ data/GFDPSP2.GSC -> GFDPSP2.GSC so Fios open/read/size path and CPK member lookup already serve real game files; crash after LOADCLEAR BADMEM guest va=0x00000020 block=0x811EFBE6 that block computes r0=*(uint32_t*)(0x816CC630+0x944) global 0x816CCF74 then dereferences [r0+0x20]; global NULL because guest GXM shader-patcher/context setup that should have stored it never ran in normal path LOADCLEAR hack forces Fios state machine before setup completes; guest wrappers confirmed 0x81207308 p=malloc(0x20) CreateLwMutex(p,name,...) *ctx=p return ignored 0x8120732C/330 LwMutex delete wrapper DeleteLwMutex + free 0x81207344/352 Lock/Unlock wrappers 0x812B2830/28A0 0x811EFB80 guest GSC program-registration path; real blocker is ordering/state machine of boot not file layer Fios load must complete as part of guest own sequence after GXM/shaders initialized which is exactly why force-clearing bit1 breaks; NEXT stop hacking bit1 instead make guest natural load path run by giving worker threads correct execution while main thread polls GFd task i.e. implement cooperative poll + punch pending async op model from old runtime its n_io_pread/Fios HLE ran completion synchronously and guest poller thread observed it; concretely instrument which thread is supposed to run FUN_811E5928 Fios step in old runtime and replicate that scheduling; also fetch/mount vita.cpk for completeness."),
    ("18.4237", "★★★★ the GFd task wait is a Fios async file-load state machine - identified exactly, and the app-run bit1 branch controls whether it runs; FUN_811E5928 locks LwMutex 0x816CC630+0x1400 wrappers 0x81207344/81207352 switches on task state [r6+2] 0..8 drives Fios state1 sprintf path HLE 0x812B2280 + sceFiosFHOpen 0x812B19F0 state2 OpIsDone/OpGetError/OpDelete/FHGetSize 1960/19E0/1A10/1A00 state4 FHRead 19D0 state5 OpCancel 1990 state7 OpWait/OpDelete/FHClose 1980/1A10/19C0 state6 done written at 0x811E5A9A movs r0,#6 strh r0,[r6,#2] exactly the condition main wait loop 0x811E5EC2 polls; main loop calls this state machine ONLY in [0x816CC630]&2==0 branch (blr 0x811E5928) with bit1 set it calls thread-mgr helper 0x81207632 instead; EXPERIMENT new P5D_LOADCLEAR=1 clears app-run bit1 at 0x816CC630 after 200 wait-loop spins vs default 100M makes state machine run reaches file-system code new PC ring 811D9E36 811D9E3A 811D9E4A 811DA534 811E6A08 812B22A0 811E6A0E 811DA53A but exits 3 with BADMEM=2 naive bit1 clear NOT the answer bit1 must be cleared through proper guest completion path; old-runtime cross-check BIT1-SET via 0x81198A76 oldflags=0 lr=0x81206760 and old runtime opened app0:/data/vita.cpk and app0:/data/data.cpk via SceIO before loading; default 30M with new opt-in switch stable exit=0 BADMEM=0 GXM=12 FSW=16; NEXT instrument Fios HLE calls inside LOADCLEAR run which open/read/size/poll calls happen what paths then implement real Fios semantics mapping app0:/data/vita.cpk + app0:/data/data.cpk to local dumped data directory instead of synthetic buffers state machine should then complete state 6 naturally and clear bit1 through guest code path."),
    ("18.4236", "★★★★ Cri handshake and GFd task-wait loop fully disassembled - the main thread is waiting for a GFd task whose job was never posted and the missing architectural piece is generic guest-callback invocation; disassembly FUN_81173288=Cri event-create sceKernelCreateEventFlag(name=event attr=0x1000) then str r0,[r4]; FUN_811732AE=Cri event-wait WaitEventFlag(*[r0],bits=1,mode=2 CLEAR,timeout=NULL) exactly the two blocked Cri threads; FUN_811732C6=Cri event-SIGNAL SetEventFlag(*[r0],1) never reached in our run; FUN_8127BD34=CriCond create eventflag attr 0 init 0; FUN_8127BE36=CriCond signal helper if r0==0 assert else SetEventFlag(*r0,1); FUN_8127BE58=generic thread-create wrapper entry 0x8127C1D2 via sceKernelCreateThread; main thread actual wait loop 0x811E5EC2 ldrsh r0,[r4,#2] cmp r0,#6 beq done DelayThread(0x1e) if ([0x816CC630]&2) bl 0x81207632 else bl 0x811E5928 b loop polls GFd task state until state==6 finished and the task job never runs because six GFd workers blocked on gfdJobCountSema and SIG2 SignalSema zero; also identified from old runtime it stores GXM displayQueueCallback from sceGxmInitialize and invokes it per display-queue entry via executor->call_guest(cb,arg,budget) n_gxm_display_entry eboot_probe.cpp:1515-1540 our harness has no generic guest-callback invocation which will also be needed for timers/audio/display callbacks once rendering starts; NEXT (1) put TASKPROBE at block 0x811E5EC6 previous insertion anchor did not match to read GFd task state/waiters (2) find who must set state=6 / post GFd job static scan for writers of task state + old-runtime log GFD/JOB flow (3) design p5d_call_guest(fn,args,budget) in harness nested run_guest with fresh RecState + explicit LR sentinel since old runtime needed it for display callbacks; default 30M stable exit=0 BADMEM=0 GXM=12 FSW=16."),
    ("18.4235", "★★★★ all guest sync objects and worker threads now mapped to subsystems by name - the stall is a boot-phase handshake not a missing HLE feature; new creation probes EFCREATE/SCREATE/TCREATE2 map semas gfdJobCountSema init 0 x3 + gfdJobEmptySema init 512/10240/8 x3 + gfdSema init 1 lr 0x812073DA created by Gfd job system lr 0x811E60AC/0x811E60C6/0x812073DA eventflags gfdJobEventFlag x3 lr 0x811E60DC event x2 lr 0x811732A0 FUN_81173288 source refs appSound/appTouch/app CriCond lr 0x8127BD8C FUN_8127BD34 kernel/sequences/app-sta threads six Gfd job workers entry 0x811E68C9 prio 0x10000100 stack 0x19000 lr 0x811E613C blocking on three gfdJobCountSema; three Cri threads entry 0x81207632 create wrapper lr 0x812074E4 prio 0xBF stacks 0x14000/0x1000/0x1000 tids 0x40017/0x40018/0x40019 two of them 0x40018/0x40019 block forever on the two event flags; one late thread 0x4001A entry 0x8127C1D2 created by FUN_8127BE58 wrapper stack 0x2000; main thread repeatedly calls CriCond signal helper FUN_8127BE36 ldr r0,[r0] movs r1,#1 blx sceKernelSetEventFlag running a Cri/CriFs condition handshake create cond at FUN_8127BD34 signal it in FUN_8127BE36 while two Cri threads wait on per-thread event flags; nothing sets those event flags because guest code that hands work to Cri threads comes after this handshake; guest boot-phase sequencing not HLE gap; NEXT trace which guest code completes CriCond wait who waits on CriCond what FUN_8127BAxx does disassemble FUN_81173288/FUN_811732AE Cri thread create/wait wrapper and FUN_8127BE58 thread create wrapper around 0x8127C1D2 identify condition main thread waits for then job system posts work and wakes Gfd workers; default 30M stable exit=0 BADMEM=0 GXM=12 FSW=16."),
    ("18.4234", "★★★★ WaitEventFlag semantics fixed old-runtime mode bitfield and the next blocker identified two guest threads wait forever on eventflags 0x60014000/0x60015000 that nothing ever sets; old-runtime n_wait_eventflag semantics recovered mode is a bitfield bit0 = OR otherwise AND bit2 = CLEAR clear only waited bits bit4 = CLEAR_ALL on success the CURRENT pattern is written to resultp not requested bits on failure the thread blocks and is replayed; harness case 0x812B2880 rewritten to exactly that mode-aware evaluate CLEAR/CLEAR_ALL result=cur main-thread path pumps workers and retries up to 2000 times plus Wake-on-SetEventFlag now honours each waiter OR/AND mode HThread.wait_mode; new EVW probe in 30M only 2 WaitEventFlag calls happen at all wait obj=60014000 bits=00000001 mode=2 cur=00000000 ok=0 thr=40018000 lr=811732C2 and wait obj=60015000 bits=1 mode=2 cur=0 ok=0 thr=40019000 lr=811732C2 both threads block forever because no code guest or HLE ever calls SetEventFlag for 0x60014000/0x60015000; meanwhile main thread still repeats SetEventFlag(0x60016000, bit1) at lr=8127BE56 and SIG2 SignalSema remains 0; next missing link is the eventflag setter for the 0x60014000/0x60015000 subsystem identify threads 0x40018000/0x40019000 creation entry/lr and guest code at lr 0x811732C2 then find which subsystem must set those flags candidates audio out/NGS voice output video decode output or display vblank notification all currently stubs returning 0 without ever setting events; default 30M stable exit=0 BADMEM=0 GXM=12 FSW=16; NEXT add CreateEventFlag creation-lr probe map eflag ids to creating subsystem identify threads 0x40018/0x40019 entries from create/start logs then implement the real event set from corresponding HLE subsystem."),
    ("18.4233", "★★★★ worker threads are not supposed to run yet - they wait on job-queue semaphores that only a job post from the guest main thread can signal and our main thread never gets there; new targeted traces SEM2/SIG2/EVT2 all six guest workers block exactly as designed at SEM2 wait obj=50011000/50013000/50015000 need=1 have=0 thr=40011xxx..40016000 lr=811E68FC thread dispatcher 0x811E68C8 retry loop and in whole 30M run SIG2 count ZERO nothing ever calls sceKernelSignalSema so workers stay blocked forever; main thread instead repeats EVT2 set obj=60016000 bits=00000001 thr=00000000 lr=8127BE56 the 0x8127BE36 CriFs/scheduler wait loop; cross-check old runtime log confirms design it creates same job queues JOBQ q=0xA0039000 [0]=0x11 total=512 q=0xA005A000 [0]=0x14 total=10240 q=0xA0115000 [0]=0x17 total=8 its workers first SEMA Wait BLOCK uid=0x11/0x14/0x17 have=0 and only later guest progress produces EVT Set/Wake and job processing old log guest threads 0x6001..0x6011 actually run; missing link NOT worker pump it is the guest main-thread boot path CriFs/loader wait loop 0x8127BE36 -> 0x812B2AE0 SetEventFlag eventflag 0x60016000 that must advance to the code which initializes job objects and posts jobs; also verified harness stub->NID mapping correct 0x812B27A0=0x0C7B834B sceKernelWaitSema 0x812B27C0=0x1BD67366 sceKernelCreateSema 0x812B2880=0x83C0E2AF sceKernelWaitEventFlag 0x812B2890=0x8516D040 sceKernelCreateEventFlag 0x812B2AD0=0xE6B761D1 sceKernelSignalSema 0x812B2AE0=0xEC94DFF7 sceKernelSetEventFlag; NEXT inspect eventflag 0x60016000 waiter who consumes bits=1 and what HLE WaitEventFlag returns then either make main-thread wait loop observe satisfied condition or find which HLE call in boot path returns wrong value keeps it spinning; then jobs can be posted and workers will start."),
    ("18.4232", "★★★★ two real HLE bugs fixed CreateSema/CreateEventFlag read the wrong argument register and the worker threads now run but the frame loop still does not start; evidence with worker tracing P5D_THRTRACE=1 inside hle_thr_pump each guest worker starts at entry 0x811E68C8 runs blocks 0x811E68C8/0x811E68D8/0x811E68EE/0x811E68F2 then calls pc=812B27A0 lr=811E68FC r0=50011000 HLE sceKernelWaitSema where it blocks forever its sema count was wrong; root cause from hle-diff report sceKernelCreateSema(name,attr,initCount,maxCount) has initCount in r2 but our HLE used r1(attr) same for sceKernelCreateEventFlag(name,attr,initPattern,opt) initPattern is r2 both fixed 18.4232; after fix enabling worker pump P5D_THRPUMP=1 makes a worker run 100+ blocks instead of blocking at once tid=40017000 pc=81207612 -> 811F2376 -> 811F22BC -> 812B2A50 DelayThread r0=5000 -> 8120760C THRBLK trace 153 lines before cap; but framectr still 0 gxm(b/e/p)=0/0/0 main loop still sits in scheduler FRAMEDUMP pc=812B27B0 blk=8120764C fib=848468E0 so workers run a DelayThread loop without driving the game world; DEFAULT CONFIG STABLE 30M exit=0 BADMEM=0 GXM=12 FSW=16 pump/trace disabled by default new env P5D_THRPUMP=1/P5D_THRTRACE=1 opt-in; NEXT identify what worker 40017000 loop 0x811F22BC..0x811F2376 waits for and who posts its jobs main thread job queue then promote safe-point pump to default once state machine correct."),
    ("18.4231", "★★★ safe-point thread pump + per-thread TLS experiment workers finally run but still make no progress reverted to M685 baseline; changes tried (1) guest worker threads get a real per-thread TLS object at r9 hle_malloc(0x400) zeroed in sceKernelStartThread Vita user threads expect r9=TLS base (2) hle_thr_pump gate relaxed to only g_cur_thr no g_in_fiber_exec (3) a SAFE-POINT pump at the fiber_exec dispatch-loop top after previous block returned before next dispatch only when g_thr_needpump && !g_cur_thr && g_blkcnt_total>1.5M instead of pumping from inside HLE (4) DelayThread requests the pump flag; RESULT workers now do get pumped THRYIELD safe-point pump 6 attempts but run still ends framectr=0 gxm(b/e/p)=0/0/0 pc=812B27B0 blk=8120764C fib=848468E0 and 31 HLE-BADMEM hle access va=60016000 blk=812B2AE0 lines these come from diagnostic probe reading the eventflag ID 0x60016000 through GP IDs are not guest VAs probe noise but also show workers reaching SetEventFlag path without advancing frame loop run time rose 37s->49s; DECISION no measurable progress experiment reverted harness restored from recomp_harness_4230.cpp reverified 30M exit=0 BADMEM=0 GXM=12 FSW=16 frames=6000 samples FRAMEDUMP pc=812B27B0 blk=8120764C fib=848468E0 gxm(b/e/p)=0/0/0; LESSON pumping workers necessary but not sufficient must first understand what each worker thread does old runtime ran guest threads as real host threads n_thread_yield + sched_pick with per-thread registers/stack so TLS bootstrap entry signature blocking protocol must be ported precisely blind run the pump only executes workers in state guest main loop does not expect; NEXT (1) instrument hle_thr_pump to trace each worker thread first 20 blocks entry lr HLE calls compare old runtime thread bootstrap n_ldtls/r9 thread entry args r0=arglen r1=argp (2) fix EVTSET2 probe to not GP eventflag IDs (3) then re-try pumping only the specific worker needed by CriFs wait loop 0x8127BE36 instead of all 7."),
