    ("18.4204", "★★★★ old GXM->Vulkan backend now LINKED into static-AOT harness: compiled 5 modules gxm_sce.o 86KB sce_gxm.cpp gxm_vk.o 300KB vulkan_backend.cpp -include cmath gxm_tex.o mem_addrspace.o 51KB common_log.o; linked recomp_harness.cpp + batch_*.o -lvulkan-1 -lgdi32 -luser32 link exit=0 exe 54,564,375 bytes; 5 bridge symbols implemented in harness p5d_last_exec_pc()=g_cur_block p5d_guest_lr() p5d_guest_reg(int) p5d_t_since_start() p5d_t_mark(const char*) [VKMARK] log common/log.cpp provides g_log_level; SMOKE TEST pathology 30M run produced 1.4 GB stdout with [NULLDESC] 2,947,635 times in first 3M lines NULLDESC guard skip null-descriptor length provider 0x811DE912 return 0 turns crash into infinite retry loop loader conversion/wait path retries forever because skipped call never delivers data it waits for run hangs no progress direct empirical proof M660 conclusion semantic patch stack XSKIP/REFNULL/NULLOBJ/RET1/RETFAM/DUMMYPROG/NULLDESC converts crashes into hangs must be replaced by correct state not extended backend dormant not cause no GXM call routed yet; NEXT (1) revert semantic patch stack to clean baseline only AOT/HLE correctness fixes kept document removed guard (2) investigate wait condition at caller of 0x811DE912 conversion path so real data producer runs rather than skipping (3) wire GXM HLE stubs through _gxm_table.csv + ABI wrappers linked backend initialize let real objects replace dummy"),
    ("18.4203", "★★★★★ old GXM->Vulkan backend link-ready under current toolchain: sce_gxm.cpp 86,179 B obj exit=0; vulkan_backend.cpp 300,724 B obj exit=0 with -include cmath one benign warning p5d_movie_layer_active initialized and declared extern; texture_format.cpp exit=0; address_space.cpp 51,000 B obj exit=0; link test g++ empty_main.cpp + objs -lvulkan-1 -lgdi32 -luser32 only 5 undefined symbols g_log_level p5d_guest_lr p5d_guest_reg p5d_last_exec_pc p5d_t_mark trivial globals guest debug state already exists in harness plus memory bridge; memory bridge register harness guest regions mem::register_region(0x80600000,0x4000000,gp_img+0) (0x84600000,0x8000000,gp_img+0x4000000) (0x8C600000,0x14000000,gp_img+0x10000000) (0xA0000000,0x2000000,gp_img+0x28000000) so mem::translate returns pointers our GP returns backend reads/writes live guest memory; ABI adapter harness GXM stubs call old typed functions pointer params guest VA->host via translate/GP integers pass through return->r0 _gxm_table.csv provides stub-VA<->function mapping; release compliance note all sources our own code allowed in release (unlike game data M662)"),
