    ("18.4201", "★★★★ old GXM backend integration feasibility confirmed (a) src/gxm/texture_format.cpp compiles cleanly MinGW g++ -std=c++17 -Isrc -Isrc/common -Isrc/loader -Isrc/gxm -Ithird_party/vulkan/include exit=0 (b) Vulkan headers present third_party/vulkan/include/vulkan/vulkan.h (c) public API p5d::vulkan::begin_frame() end_frame() present_frame(colorData) materialize_fragment_textures(const void* const controls[16]) g_backend state; ABI convention decoded from src/gxm/sce_gxm.cpp handlers receive host pointers directly sceGxmTextureInitLinear writes through pointer old interpreter import bridge pre-translated guest VAs to host pointers adapter must translate RecState args via GP() before calling typed function write back r0; backend deps mem::translate/contains 19 uses common/log.h Windows/Vulkan helper p5d_gxm_pack_texture p5d_gxm_fill_fragment_controls gxm_draw_arrays; integration recipe (1) build sce_gxm.cpp + vulkan_backend.cpp + texture_format.cpp into static-AOT harness (2) implement mem::translate shim over GP() register guest image region (3) generate per-function ABI wrappers from src/gxm/sce_gxm.h prototypes pointer args GP ints passthrough return r0 route harness 0x812B1xxx GXM stubs through _gxm_table.csv (4) initialize backend from harness call begin/end/present at game frames (5) keep stubs only for unimplemented; replaces dummy GXM objects real ones removes null +0x20 chain at source"),
    ("18.4200", "★★★★★ path correction audit previous native runtime source tree still exists and contains a real GXM->Vulkan backend current static-AOT harness never reused: C:/dev/p5dsrc/src/gxm/vulkan_backend.cpp 409,022 bytes 5,694 lines sce_gxm.cpp 60,262 bytes 167 SceGxm functions texture_format.cpp 23,451 bytes src/arm 64 files ARM interpreter src/assets 207 files scene renderers p5d_render_core.h 93 KB src/audio filesystem kernel loader 37 files mem usse; _gxm_table.csv NID<->Name<->stub VA 0x812Bxxxx<->native handler e.g. 008402C6 sceGxmMapFragmentUsseMemory 812B11C0 n_gxm_map_usse, 14BD831F sceGxmSetFrontDepthFunc 812B1260 n_gxm_ok; _nidcall_gxm.txt real call counts 133,649 calls to 0xA949A803, 116,329 to 0x277794C4, 18,428 to 0x14BD831F; bin/p5d_play.exe out_build/p5d_title_screen.exe milestone PNGs milestone_vk_frame_lifecycle milestone_texture_sampling old runtime really reached Vulkan frame rendering; C:/dev/p5d_native/src is only a demo project main.cpp OBJ viewer player.cpp BMP frame player p5d_game.cpp fake BOOT/TITLE/MENU/GAME state machine rendering BMPs not the GXM backend; correct conclusion route correction backend exists substantial but lives in OLD runtime must be integrated into static-AOT harness; current ad-hoc semantic patch stack XSKIP/REFNULL/NULLOBJ/RET1/RETFAM/DUMMYPROG/NULLDESC should be cleaned up; NEXT (1) use _gxm_table.csv bridge map harness 0x812B1xxx GXM stubs to old native functions generate ABI shim copying RecState registers/stack into typed C arguments (2) build src/gxm/sce_gxm.cpp + vulkan_backend.cpp + texture_format.cpp into harness adapt mem/address_space to GP() guest memory and common/log (3) replace GXM stubs real backend where implemented stub only unimplemented (4) re-run boot path null +0x20 chain render-side traversal get real objects instead of fabricated ones"),
    ("18.4199", "★★★★ fabricated NULLOBJ pollutes draw traversal real problem divergence from reference run: (1) pump-loop variant of [obj+0x20] source substitution fired 8x [DUMMYPROG] creator +0x20 <- 85033450 (pump) covers fiber2 loop; (2) draw traversal still skips [RET1] skip FUN_811e2b50 model+0x20 null r1=85349640 lr=811AD9C2; new [CHAIN] dump sl=85349640 A=[sl+0x40]=85348D70 B=[A+0x78]=8534B230 B+0x20=00000000 and B=0x8534B230 lies INSIDE NULLOBJ scratch allocation 0x8534B220+0x10 fabricated dummy taken as real object downstream pointer dummy+0x10 stored into A+0x78; NULLOBJ fabrication propagates garbage model/material chain cannot be fixed by more substitutions; (3) old reference logs never execute creator FUN_811c40dc 0x811C40 hits=0 all reference traces but our run does boot diverges into path working reference never takes; NEXT find divergence instrument creator call chain 0x811B467C/0x811B49F0 compare call sequence old reference [N2X] backtraces expected route OR drop fabricated dummies seed resource registry lookup hits properly built object creator clone path refs [r6+0x20]; draw traversal proven reachable divergence last obstacle before render loop"),
