    ("18.4196", "★★★★ M655 runtime-code-patch hypothesis REFUTED [EF2] probe guest memory at 0x811EFE9A byte-identical to ELF 00 20 70 47 | 2D E9 F0 4F movs r0,#0 bx lr followed by real 542-byte function 0x811EFE9E game really calls 0-returning stub; block 0x811E3520 r0=[r4+0x20] r2=sp bl 0x811F01AE [EF2] site=0 r4=8534B160 [r4+0x20]=0 enter F01AE r0=0 lr=811E3528 after F01AE r0=00000004; FUN_811F01AE decoded push sub sp,#0x1c r7=r0 r8=r2 r2=[r8] if r2 != 0xF goto else if r1 < 4 r0=(r1*4-r1) r0=r7+(r0<<2) r0+=4 return i.e. r1=0 returns r7+4 source+4 null source -> address 4 next block 0x811E3528 ldr r0,[r4] BADMEM va=0x4 block=0x811E3528; crash explained genuine 0-returning stub feeds NULL into resource factory returns NULL+4 dereferenced; NEXT decide dev/tool-only bypass check flags/branches 0x811C40E0 0x811E34xx or fabricate minimal non-null PFSG-like source object or find other branch normally sets [obj+0x20]; old dynamic-recompilation phase logs may show real hardware path"),
    ("18.4195", "★★★★★ BL target is genuinely a 4-byte stub movs r0,#0 bx lr at 0x811EFE9A (function_bounds FUN_811efe9a size 4; real 542-byte GXM loader function starts 0x811EFE9E): manual Thumb BL decode of creator call bytes 2b f0 bc fe at 0x811C411E gives target 0x811C4122+0x2BD78=0x811EFE9A game really calls function returning 0; either (a) 4-byte stub patched at runtime code patch/self-modifying code static AOT never sees AOT generated from ELF file while guest may patch code memory during boot (b) stub linker/weak placeholder runtime fixup overwrites (c) game tolerates 0 and null chain from different bug; evidence generated block 0x811C411C r0=r6 lr=0x811C4122 return 0x811EFE9A correct lr target matches manual decode next block 0x811C4122 stores r0 into [r5+0x20] exactly observed single write [OBJ20W] a=8534B180 v=0 blk=811C4122; NEXT compare GUEST MEMORY at 0x811EFE9A after boot with ELF bytes 00 20 70 47 [EFE9A] probe inserted only into BlockFn fn=gbn(pc) dispatch sites 6 occurrences none executed for this block so next round also into fiber2 pump loop f2fn and thread pump; if guest bytes differ runtime code patch must add interpreter fallback for patched code regions objective explicitly requires AOT + interpreter fallback; if identical look for intended producer of +0x20 resource elsewhere"),
