    ("18.4190", "★★★★★ 0x8121D044 spin was two AOT shift bugs in generator both fixed (1) register-shift amounts masked &0x1F so lsrs r1,r1,fp at fp=32 wrapped to shift 0 kept r1 nonzero forever loop 0x8121D044 bit-length scan r1>>=fp bne; fix emits (_sh>=32u)?0u:(v>>_sh) for LSL/LSR sign-fill ASR proper rotate ROR 3-reg 2-reg immediate forms immediate LSR/ASR #0 now means #32 Thumb encoding (2) 3-register shift forms did not emit setf_nz so following bne tested STALE flags - now they do (18.4190b); after full regen 26/26 ok relink 0x8121D044 spin GONE 0 occurrences instead of ~1.2M lines fiber2 advanced from bit-scan into 0x8121D0CC then memory-block/GXM setup [MEMA] AllocMemBlock uid=00000136 size=00040000 addr=850ACB70 [MEMB] GetMemBlockInfo uid=00000136 -> base=850ACB70 same uid=0x137 HLE ring 812B29F0@812077AC 812B29E0@81207802 812B1640@81207820 812B2830@81207350 812B28A0@8120735C AllocMemBlock -> GetMemBlockInfo -> 812B1640; NEW BLOCKER native access violation exit=0xC0000005 ~895,270 blocks 9s right after those HLE calls no BADMEM crash inside HLE stubs on path most likely 0x812B1640 or memblock-info writes; NEXT inspect HLE case 0x812B1640 and stubs after it in ring unsafe pointer access/size add guard/print re-run loader now deeper MemBlock allocation for GXM surfaces next unblock toward frame loop"),
    ("18.4189", "★★★★★ root cause of bad-pointer cascade found and fixed HLE 0x812B2280 path/string formatter returned DESTINATION POINTER instead of NUMBER OF BYTES WRITTEN: caller 0x811C6584 does r5 += r0 advance by returned length with our dst return r5 doubled each of 46 loop iterations [PFMT] #1 r0=09FD8440 #2 r0=13FB0880 #3 r0=27F61100 #4 r0=4FEC2200 doubling chain fmt '#define %s %s.' shader-preprocessor macro building produced 3027 [HLE-BADMEM] lines in one 30M run corrupted GXP/shader-compilation path; FIX HLE case computes oi formatted length returns r0=oi_out added [PFMT2] trace dst fmt oi ret; RESULT [PFMT2] dst=82EFFDA8 fmt=8130C6C4 oi=15 ret=15 oi=102 ret=102 correct BADMEM lines 3027 -> 0 30M exit=0; new progress formatter fixed fiber2 pump advances past byte-swap/matrix-init into NEW region 0x8121D044 [P2PROG] pass=29500..29800 pc=8121D044 lr=0x80 r1=0 GXP shader preprocessor/compiler path running XSKIP3 4x FLPROBE=0 frames=0 GXM=12; NEXT instrument 0x8121D044 loop which function what waits continue unblocking shader-compile/GXM path loader finishes frame loop reached"),
    ("18.4188", "★★★★ diagnostic bypass of runaway endian conversion works converter entered with length 0xFFFFFFFF skipped r2->0 XSWAPSKIP/XSKIP3 fired 4x 30M run completes exit=0 no more BADMEM at 0xA2000000; next blocker [HLE-BADMEM] hle access va=09FD8440 blk=812B2280 ring 811C652E repeated path/formatter HLE 0x812B2280 called from new region 0x811C65xx unmapped destination pointer 0x09FD8440 far below all mapped ranges may be truncated pointer 0xA0xxxxxx top byte lost; guard inside [XSWAP] probe at converter entry 0x811DD4BC if r2==0xFFFFFFFF r2=0 converter returns immediately count 0; tooling note badly-written regex deleted part of thread-pump loop harness restored from tools_backup/recomp_harness_4187.cpp guard re-applied exact anchors keep precise anchor style; NEXT trace destination pointer source 0x811C652E path formatting fix truncated guest pointer high byte lost or unmapped scratch buffer map region continue matrix-init/frame loop"),
    ("18.4187", "★★★★ object 0x84CE12B0 write watch game object with fiber-like field block +0x84..+0x98 but size field +0x90 callback#3 returns NEVER WRITTEN in 30M blocks and +4 stays list self-link: added [OBJH] range write-watch 0x84CE12B0..0x84CE1370 inside wr32_watch captured init history +4=0x84CE12DC blk 0x811E5DEE self+0x2C list link; blk 0x811E5DFA +0xB8=0xFFFFFFFF +0xBC=0 +0xC0=0 +0xC4=0 +0xD0=0xFFFFFFFF; blk 0x81207290 +0xC8=1 +0xCC=1; blk 0x811E5E3A/48 +0xD4=0 +0xD8=0; fiber-like block +0x84=0x84CE1350 +0x88=0x84CE1350 blk 0x8115F458 +0x8c=0x84CE1460 +0x94=0 +0x98=4 blk 0x8115D256 appGxModel/GxModel region; NO write to +0x90 size callback 0x8118308A returns and +4 never becomes 3 stays list link callback#3 keeps returning 0 descriptor zero size; NEXT find code sets +0x90 and/or state +4==3 completion step of task whose entry +0x84=0x8115D7BF appGxModel region make producer run callback#3 real size 0x811DE912 real length endian conversion completes"),
