    ("18.4185", "★★★★ FUN_811DEAB4 / 0x811DE912 fully decoded -1 from type-3 path because descriptor +0x18/+0x1c zero [struct+0x1c] end ptr <= [struct+0x18] current ptr r3 stays -1 return: [OBJ24] probes pc=811DEAB4 r0=3 r1=1 r2=A05FFDB8 lr=811C6C90 FUN_811DEAB4 type=3 flags=1 ptr=&stack-size malloc(0x24) memset 0 stores +0x10=type 0003 +0x12=flags 0001 if type>0 stores +0x18=*ptr ptr=A05FFDB8 fiber2 stack slot; then pc=811DEB34 r4=84FEC040 struct 00000000 x4 00010003 00000000 x5 i.e. +0x18=0 +0x1c=0 +0x20=0 and pc=811DEB44 r0=FFFFFFFF confirms 0x811DE912 returned -1; decoded 0x811DE912 len=[r6+0x10] type 3 checks r5=[r6+0x18] vs lr=[r6+0x1c] cmp r5,lr bhs keep r3=-1 r4=r3 return r4 both fields 0 returns -1 immediately; size argument from *ptr=[A05FFDB8] is 0 caller lr=0x811C6C90 0x811C6Cxx render/model callback passed zero size; NEXT trace caller 0x811C6C8x where size should come from likely CPK file read/size query returning 0 [CONSUME] FHRead calls=1 bytes=62100 far too little for full boot fix file-read/size path descriptor real size endian conversion completes"),
    ("18.4184", "★★★★ runaway endian conversion explained converter called with length r2=0xFFFFFFFF (-1) because length provider 0x811DE912 takes return -1 path struct field [r6+0x12] bit0 is 0: [XSWAP] probe block 0x811DD4BC r0=84FEC040 r1=84FEC040 r2=FFFFFFFF r3=FFFFFFFF r4=84FEC040 r5=A05FFDB8 lr=811DEB4E sp=A05FFDA0 fib=84846860 struct header hdr +0=0 +0x18=0 +0x1c=0; call site 0x811DEB3A r0=r4 r1=r4 r2=0x10 bl 0x811DE912 -> r2=r0 returned length -> 0x811DEB46 r0=r4 r1=r4 r2=length bl 0x811DD4BC converter; decode 0x811DE912 r6=r0 r4=r2 r7=r1 r0=ldrh [r6+0x12] r0&=1 if r0==0 r0=-1 return so bit0 of struct+0x12 zero returns -1 caller passes straight to converter loops count 0xFFFFFFFF walking r0 upward until leaves Region B at 0xA2000000 harness BADMEM; M643 unbounded length really -1 sentinel from uninitialized/invalid structure descriptor struct 0x84FEC040 +0x12 flag clear size fields zero asset descriptor not populated by loader before conversion; NEXT trace who allocates/fills struct 0x84FEC040 caller above 0x811DEB34 which load/decompress step sets [struct+0x12] bit0 likely file-read/decode HLE returns short leaves descriptor zero fix so length provider returns real length conversion completes matrix init frame loop"),
    ("18.4183", "★★★★★ two major fixes (1) AOT generator dropped POST-INDEX WRITEBACK on ldr/str str r3,[r0],#4 emitted only store never r0+=4 fixed for ldr/ldrb/ldrh/ldrsh/ldrsb/ldrd str/strb/strh/strd post-index imm/reg and pre-index disp (2) Region B extended 16MB->32MB fresh host offset 0x28000000 harness GP + generator P + full regen: writeback visible regenerated block 0x811DD4E0 wr32(s,s->r[0]+0,s->r[3]); s->r[0]=s->r[0]+4; previously r0+=4 missing endian byte-swap loop 0x811DD4C8-0x811DD4E6 kept writing same word; after fix conversion advances and walks UP THROUGH Region B until end of mapping [BADMEM] va=0xA1000000 block=0x811DD4C8 -> after Region B 32MB becomes [BADMEM] va=0xA2000000 block=0x811DD4C8 conversion unbounded/too long length arg or end pointer wrong not merely out of range; tooling pitfalls generator patch added second out = [] broke _gen_split.py main_idx marker renamed _wbo and _wb used o.base instead of o.mem.base; current 30M exit=3 95s fiber2 still byte-swap inner loop pass 24,000 [P2PROG] pass=24000 pc=811DD4D0 lr=811DEB4E r1=0 FLPROBE=0 frames=0 GXM=12; NEXT probe converter entry block 0x811DD4BC log r0/r1/r2 buffer start/end/length caller lr=0x811DEB4E decide larger memblock/Region B or length corrupted let conversion complete reach matrix-init/frame loop"),
    ("18.4182", "★★★★ after missing-function fix run stable at long lengths 8M/18s 30M/59s 100M exit=0 ZERO BADMEM and fiber2 advances through byte-swap into matrix-init loop 0x811EAAE4 but frame loop still not reached FLPROBE=0 frames=0 GXM=12: pump-tuning (a) larger pump budget 60000 blocks/150ms/cooldown200 REGRESSED 30M 399s exit=3 fiber2 back to 0x811830CC state wait reverted budget8000/40ms/cooldown4000 (b) periodic pump trigger (n%20000)==0 in addition to block 0x811E5CDA gave 50M 100s exit=0 ZERO BADMEM FLPROBE/frames 0; fiber2 after wait executes endian byte-swap helper 0x811DD4BC ldr r1,[r0] lsrs r3,r1,#24 bfi str r3,[r0],#4 converts 32-bit words then matrix initialization loop 0x811EAAE4 ldr r0,[r7,0x304] ldr r0,[r0] str r2=0x3F800000 str r2,[r0,#4/#8/#c] subs lr,lr,#1 bne 0x811EAAE4 lr=0x00048400 295,936 iterations 16-byte writes loader material/bone matrix init; NEXT instrument pump passes unbounded log saved fiber2 r15/lr/r1 current SEQ capped 60 verify matrix loop advances iteration-by-iteration across passes fix pump context save/restore r1/lr if not raise pump duty cycle complete ~296k matrix iterations frame loop 0x81198C8E reached"),
    ("18.4181", "★★★★★ stall was indirect-miss on four functions missing from function_bounds.json - adding them makes 8M run complete in 18s ZERO BADMEM no freeze: traced [HARNESS] indirect miss at pc=811E5C98 to callback trampoline 0x811E5C98 callback table 0x81513DD4..0x81513DE8 = 81182C57/8118307B/81182F6B/8118308B/811830C9/81182F1D invoked entry 0x8118308B Thumb pointer of function 0x8118308A NO translated block; same 0x81182F1C 0x81182F6A 0x8118307A real functions push prologues reached only indirectly; FIX appended 4 entries function_bounds.json 0x81182F1C size 0x4E 0x81182F6A size 0x110 0x8118307A size 0x10 state==3 predicate ldrsh r0,[r0,4] cmp r0,3 beq->1 else 0 0x8118308A size 0x3E canary-framed wait/lock helper regenerated all 26 batches 26/26 ok 412s; RESULT indirect miss GONE 8M exit=0 18s ZERO BADMEM no [HARNESS] break FRAMEDUMP advances all 8,000,000 blocks before froze 441,918/644,226 YMAIN=8 THR=20 flags=00000002; frame counter still 0 GXM=12 end-of-run trace still fiber scheduler loops pc=812067E8/812067A0/81198BF2 fib=848367C0 boot/load/scheduler phase now stable remaining work enter frame loop"),
    ("18.4180", "★★★★ yield-to-main unwind implemented and working fibers periodically unwind to main loop worker threads actually run THR=20; second stall site remains fiber2 pump loop triggered from block 0x811E5CDA re-enters forever without advancing main-loop counter: implemented (a) sceKernelCheckCallback 0x812B2AC0 and sceKernelDelayThread 0x812B2A50 when g_in_fex==1 every 64th yield sets g_yield_to_main instead of fiber switch (b) top of fiber_exec_to_completion loop when g_yield_to_main && g_in_fex==1 fiber_save current context break out to HLE caller restores thread returns to guest main loop (c) fiber2 pump loop nested-progress guard g_blkcnt_total delta > 200000 or g_yield_to_main break; RESULT 8M run 31s was 60s [YMAIN] request from CheckCallback fib=848367C0 pc=812B2AC0 [YMAIN] unwind fiber=848367C0 pc=81198BF2 [YMAIN] request from DelayThread fib=84846860 pc=812B2A50 [YMAIN] unwind fiber=84846860 pc=8120766A all fire worker threads created/started THR=20 unwind lets main loop and hle_thr_pump run; BUT run freezes n=644226 WD stall 13 HLE ring 812B2A50@81207612 repeated [PMP2B]/[PMP2C] traces fiber2 pump loop PMPBREAK=0 break never triggered pump nested progress not reflected in g_blkcnt_total; NEXT (1) post-pump fiber1 pc advance past trigger block 0x811E5CDA add pump cooldown (2) pump-break from wall-iteration/nested-exec counter instead of g_blkcnt_total (3) re-check frame counter after pump stops monopolizing"),
    ("18.4179", "★★★★★ stall watchdog reveals real architectural blocker entire fiber world runs inside ONE nested HLE call main loop never advances worker threads never run: detached host watchdog thread [WD] every 2s dumps block counter current block/fiber/thread last 12 HLE calls PC ring; with UNCOND3 diagnostic run stalls n=2,710,912 frozen stall 8..13 wall time kept going watchdog [WD] n=2710912 blk=811830CC/811830D6/8120760C/812B2A50 fib=84846860 thr=00000000 stall=13 HLE ring dominated 812B2A50@81207612 repeated sceKernelDelayThread from 0x81207612 [PMP2B] ppc=8120760C r0=00007530 sp=A05FFDA8 [PMP2C] nx=811830DE r0=0; PC ring cycles fiber1 lifecycle fiber2 delay wait scheduler blocks 81198BF6/811E5CDA/812067A0/812B1B70 and 811830CC/811830D6/8120760C/812B2A50 and 8120682A/81206832 both fibers ping-pong forever inside one HLE call main-loop block counter frozen; why worker threads starved state producers never run frame counter [0x816CC630+0xC] stays 0 even after wait state forced; NEXT implement controlled UNWIND from nested fiber execution back to main loop cooperative yield-to-main on every Nth fiber yield set flag save fiber contexts return sentinel from fiber_exec_to_completion through HLE frames let main loop run one hle_thr_pump quantum re-enter fiber world from saved context lets worker producers run game advance frame loop"),
    ("18.4178", "★★★★ wait object captured at loop body r4=0x84FEDA00 160-byte guest calloc buffer lr=0x811E6A2E state int16 at +4; diagnostic bypass reveals next blocker execution stops advancing at n~360000: [LOOP8CC] probes loop-body block 0x811830CC fiber_exec dispatch + main loop + [DWATCH] object state; RESULT [LOOP8CC] EX r4=84FEDA00 r0=0 sp=A05FFDA8 lr=81207612 fib=84846860 ring alternating 81198BF6/81198BEA/811E5CDA/812067A0/812B1B70 fiber1 lifecycle <-> 811830CC/811830D6/8120760C/812B2A50 fiber2 DelayThread(0x7530) wait <-> 8120682A/81206832 scheduler; object [CALLOC] n=160 sz=1 -> 84FEDA00 +4 state starts 0 nothing guest writes 3; diagnostic unblocking FORCE3 once did not help state reset loop re-entered ALWAYS3 capped probes did not help UNCOND3 both dispatch sites force state=3 every time block 0x811830CC reached -> UNCOND3=2 then RUN STOPPED ADVANCING FRAMEDUMP ends n~360000 last pc=812067E8 blk=812067DC pc=812B1B70 blk=812067A0 wall 59s; state wait no longer blocker control proceeds stalls in blocking HLE/fiber path last trace sceFiberGetSelf 0x812B1B70 called from fiber manager 0x812067A0; NEXT dump last HLE stubs/PC ring at stall instrument 0x812067xx fiber-manager loop and HLE call ring when no block progress for N blocks identify new blocking API continue unblocking frame loop"),
