    ("18.4164", "★★★★ boot-complete exit path decoded - app-run function 0x8120690E returns, init wrapper calls libc exit 0x81198A9E, last HLE calls are GXM program lookups: HLE-call ring [EXITLOG] dumps last 64 stubs+LRs on libc exit 0x812B22C0; RESULT [EXITLOG] libc exit called lr=81198AA2 hle_total=100775 ring tail 0x812B12A0 lr=811EFFA0 / 0x812B1530 lr=811EFF9A alternating dozens times then 0x812B1B90 lr=812069D6, 0x812B2250 lr=811E6A1E x2, finally 0x812B22C0 lr=81198AA2; static decode call site 0x81198A98 bl 0x8120690E app-run/lifecycle then 0x81198A9C ldr r0,[sp] 0x81198A9E blx 0x812B22C0 libc exit - init wrapper 0x81198A40 calls app-run 0x8120690E and when it RETURNS calls exit; our run reaches normal program-termination because 0x8120690E returns immediately instead of blocking in frame/lifecycle loop; docs identify last HLE stubs 0x812B12A0 sceGxmProgramFindParameterByName / 0x812B1530 GetProgramFromId SceGxm shader-patcher, zero returns mean shader/program path completes trivially instead of driving rendering; NEXT implement plausible GXM program/shader-patcher stubs and make 0x8120690E lifecycle wait actually block drive frame pacing from harness so app stays in frame loop -> first frame"),
    ("18.4163", "★★★★★ LARGE-BLOCK ARENA FIX - all allocator-init calls valid bases, 3M/10M exit=0 ZERO BADMEM: root cause [MEMA] AllocMemBlock uid=0000013B size=00F00000 addr=00000000 / uid=00000150 size=03200000 addr=00000000 game requests 15MB and 32MB blocks hle_malloc ran out of contiguous space heaps small even returned A0000000 inside Region-B window returned 0 GetMemBlockInfo base=0 allocator-init crash; FIX dedicated large-block arena hle_malloc requests >=1MB from bump arena VA 0x8C600000..0xA0000000 320MB mapped in batch P() and harness GP() to host offset 0x10000000 IMG_SIZE 768MB AllocMemBlock/GetMemBlockInfo log [MEMA]/[MEMB]; RESULT all seven [ALLOC] valid bases last 32MB at 0x9B899740 3M exit=0 6s ZERO BADMEM 10M exit=0 6s ZERO BADMEM; LOADCLEAR=4 RESTART2=3 THRARG=31 GXM=12 CPKNAME=25 THR=20 CHKFIX2=0; 10M trace game completed main thread + fibers pc=0 last_block=0x81206C5C idling RESTART2 3 attempts exhausted; NEXT make completed boot transition into FRAME/RENDER loop instead of restarting from scratch"),
    ("18.4162", "★★★★ MAPPED [0x9F000000,0xA0000000) 16MB Vita user-memblock window offset 0x10000000 in both batch P() and harness GP() - 0x9FE00000 fiber-stack crash GONE: generator P() prelude _gen_split.py + harness GP() branch else if (a >= 0x9F000000u && a < 0xA0000000u) off=(a-0x9F000000u)+0x10000000u; 26 batches regenerated 26/26 ok 382.6s relink; RESULT 3M 11s previous crashes GONE no BADMEM va=0x9FDFFFFC block=0x81206BDC no HLE-BADMEM va=0x9FE00000; LOADCLEAR twice THRARG=17 RESTART2=1 GXM=12 CPKNAME=25 THR=20 CHKFIX2=0 FSWSAN=0; crash moves [BADMEM] guest va=0x00000008 unmapped block=0x811C0DA8 ring_va=0x00000008 811D9FD0 811D9F9E; [ALLOC] allocator-init FUN_811C0D74 called from block 0x81207956 function 0x81207924 first call [ALLOC] enter r0=86A74E80 r1=00F00000 lr=8120795A VALID second call r0=00000000 r1=00F00000 base 0 crash [r0+8]; caller chain 0x81207924 -> FUN_81207734 memory-map helper -> HLE 0x812B29F0 AllocMemBlock / 0x812B29E0 GetMemBlockInfo descriptor field [r5+0] base written by GetMemBlockInfo uid lookup miss our HLE writes nothing descriptor stays zero; NEXT add logging AllocMemBlock/GetMemBlockInfo uid lookup hit/miss returned base fix second invocation missing base uid mismatch or extra map path 0x812B1640 returns 0"),
