    ("18.4023", "static recompilation stage 6jq: disassembled prologue before new fault - 8115D242 bl 0x8115F448 then 8115D246 mov sl,r0 -> SL is RETURN VALUE of 0x8115F448, followed by 8115D248 add sb,sl,#0x14; 8115D24C mov r0,sb; 8115D250 movs r1,#0; 8115D252 blx 0x812B2260 (memset/init of structure at sl+0x14 using size fp), then stores into [sl+0x14]/[sl+0x18]/[sl+0x1c]/[sl+0x24]/[sl+0x28]/[sl+0x2c] and array loop at [sl+0x20]; fault ldr r0,[sl+0x20] with sl=0 -> ROOT CAUSE 0x8115F448 returned 0 (structure allocation/creation failed); NEXT identify 0x8115F448 (veneer? malloc-like) and 0x812B2260 (init call) in veneer_map/harness, find why creation returns 0 (HLE allocator returns 0 for size/args or prerequisite missing), fix so structure created and array iteration proceeds"),
    ("18.4022", "static recompilation stage 6jp: analyzed NEW BADMEM after fiber-switch fix - [BADMEM] guest va=0x00000020 unmapped block=0x8115D28C ring 812B1B70 812067B6 81206...; faulting block MOVED to 0x8115D2xx region (previously 0x812068xx) - guest now executes further fiber/task code; disasm 0x8115D270 movs r8,#0; str r0,[sl,#0x1c]; str r6,[sl,#0x20]; beq; ldr r0,[sl,#0x1c]; bl 0x81173194; 0x8115D28C ldr r0,[sl,#0x20]; add r8,#1; adds r4,#8; cmp r8,r0; blo 0x8115D282; generated blk_8115D28C s->r[0]=rd32(s->r[10]+0x20) -> ARRAY-ITERATION function (r8 counter, r4 stride 8, per-element call 0x81173194, upper bound [sl+0x20]) whose structure pointer sl (=r10) is ZERO -> va=0x20; ring shows reached from fiber-manager path (GetSelf 812B1B70 -> 812067B6 -> 81206xx); NEXT disassemble function prologue before 0x8115D270 find where sl/r10 set by caller, trace caller passing sl=0, repair argument or initialize structure so iteration proceeds"),
    ("18.4021", "★★ static recompilation stage 6jo: implemented fiber FCtx auto-create on unknown target (switch handler reads fiber object [fiber+0x84] user entry and [fiber+0x88] argOnRun, calls fiber_load, retries g_fctx.find); RESULT [FIBER-AUTOCREATE] fired (t=846867F0 entry=81198C0B arg=82EFFF28) and switch now happens REPEATEDLY ([FEVT] switch cur=84676750 to=846867F0 many times, previously only once) -> switch mechanism FIXED; BUT GXM calls still 0, FIOS opens still 0, run now CRASHES again (BADMEM 2, 10M exit=3) - fiber2 execution after successful switch triggers new fault (progress-by-moving-fault pattern); NEXT capture new BADMEM details (faulting block/va and ring) from err10m_autocreate.txt, disassemble around faulting block, apply same class of repair (resume/entry precondition, missing object)"),
    ("18.4020", "★★★ static recompilation stage 6jn: FIBER SWITCH FAILING WITH unknown target = THE LOOP - 10M grep: [FEVT] switch cur=84676750 to=846867F0 runs=1 (only ONE switch ever), [SWP] fb=846867F0 in=1 cur=84676750 sp=A0DFFFE8 MANY times (sceFiberSwitch(fiber2) called repeatedly inside fiber_exec only arms g_fiber_switch_to), [FIBER-SW] unknown target 846867F0 appears; fiber1 repeatedly calls sceFiberSwitch(fiber2) deferred switch consumed by fiber_exec but g_fctx.find(fiber2) FAILS - fiber2 NOT registered in g_fctx - switch handler logs unknown target breaks and fiber1 keeps retrying forever; ROOT CAUSE fiber2 FCtx never created via fiber_load (only path that populates g_fctx for new fiber) because earlier flow created fiber OBJECT (0x81206700) but never loaded/resumed it; FIX in switch handler when target fiber missing from g_fctx CREATE its FCtx on the spot (fiber_load(s, t, entry from [fiber+0x84], arg from [fiber+0x88]) and proceed instead of breaking; NEXT implement auto-create on unknown target + 10M -> switch should succeed fiber2 task should run game should advance past fiber-manager loop"),
    ("18.4019", "★★★ static recompilation stage 6jm: DECISIVE ACTIVITY ANALYSIS of 10M run: GXM CALLS 0, FIOS OPENS 0, LOOP STARTS VERY EARLY - grep over out10m_flistfix.txt [GXM-BEGIN]/[GXM-PRESENT]/[GXM-CTX] count 0, FIOS OPEN 0, [GFX] periodic stats never appeared; FIRST [PROG] lines already fiber region n=5000 pc=8120685A last_block=812068D8 sp=82EFFE68 r0=0, n=10000 pc=812068A0 last_block=81206894, n=15000 pc=8120685A, n=20000 pc=812068A0 -> from very beginning guest cycling 0x812068xx fiber-manager region and NEVER reaches asset loading (FIOS) or rendering (GXM); CONCLUSION fiber task loop spinning WITHOUT advancing game main workflow (scheduler tasks fiber1/fiber2 per-frame work not producing progress); earlier 3M runs DID open files (57,438 FIOS opens per M428) so something added since changed flow early on (or those opens under previous crash path); NEXT determine what fiber2 task does per cycle - dump distinct pc sequence for fiber2 right after each switch (pcs executed between switch-in and switch-out); if fiber2 task empty/instant its user entry or task body not executed (wrong entry point or task returns immediately because condition/HLE result differs) which would explain zero asset/render progress"),
    ("18.4018", "static recompilation stage 6jl: read g_fiber_switch_to consumption path - fiber_exec_to_completion line 702 main loop 722 consumes deferred switch at line 726 (g_fiber_switch_to -> t; fiber_save; g_fctx.find(t); if target pc==0 restart from user entry; g_cur_fiber=t; memcpy(s->r)); NESTED-REFUSED guard 704-713; deferred switch IS consumed; REVISED busy-wait chain: fiber1 runs completion 0x812067A0 sets [fiber1+0x80]|=2 removal logic switches to head fiber2 HLE arms g_fiber_switch_to fiber_exec consumes switches fiber2 runs task finishes switch handler restarts it (738-748) or returns to fiber1 -> fiber1 completion again = repeated fiber1<->fiber2 completion loop; may be normal per-frame fiber cycle BUT [PROG] pc never leaves 0x812067xx-0x812068xx across 10M blocks -> no progress into next game phase; NEXT instrument what each fiber does per cycle (distinct pcs / FIOS opens / GXM calls per 100k blocks) see if real work happens, check fiber2 completion path - if it completes immediately its user entry (scheduler task) may be wrong"),
    ("18.4017", "static recompilation stage 6jk: tried fiber-list repair (fiber2.next=fiber1 when asymmetric): [FLISTFIX] fired 5+ times (fiber2.next 0 -> fiber1 sp=A0DFFFE8 cur=84676750 n=1..5) but game REWRITES fiber2.next back to 0 every round - repair NOT persistent because COMPLETION FUNCTION itself zeroes links as part of removing fiber; [PROG] at 10M still same fiber state region (pc=8120682A last=812B1BA0 / pc=8120680E last=81206806 / pc=812067C8 last=812067B6 / pc=81206822 last=81206820) loop did NOT exit; BADMEM 0 stable; REVISED understanding: complete/remove fiber1 -> head=fiber2 -> cmp r3,r0 NOT equal -> call sceFiberSwitch -> inside fiber_exec HLE defers via g_fiber_switch_to and returns -> fiber_exec_to_completion switch handler apparently never processes g_fiber_switch_to -> same fiber loops re-removing itself; NEXT inspect how g_fiber_switch_to consumed (fiber_exec_to_completion/dispatch loop) make deferred switch actually happen or make removed fiber stop running"),
    ("18.4016", "★★★ static recompilation stage 6jj: FIBER LIST ASYMMETRIC = ROOT CAUSE OF BUSY-WAIT - [FLIST2] at block 0x8120682A: h18=0 h1c=846867F0 (head=fiber2 non-zero) f1p=846867F0 f1n=0 f2p=0 f2n=0 r3=84676750 cur=84676750 (n=1..10); decoding global list head [0x816CBC08+0xa1c]=0x846867F0 fiber2, fiber1.prev [fiber1+0x94]=0x846867F0 fiber2, fiber1.next=0, fiber2.prev=0, fiber2.next=0, completion function running for r3=fiber1 0x84676750; BUG list ASYMMETRIC - fiber1.prev points to fiber2 but fiber2.next does NOT point back to fiber1 (0); removal logic r2=fiber1.prev=fiber2 writes as new head ([r4,#0xa1c]=0x846867F0) then compares removed fiber r3=fiber1 with new head r0=0x846867F0 NOT equal so calls sceFiberSwitch and loops forever; fiber2.next==0 list never walked to fiber1; FIX repair fiber2.next to fiber1 ([0x846867F0+0x98]=0x84676750) or keep prev/next symmetric; NEXT apply one-value list repair + 10M confirm loop exits and game proceeds"),
    ("18.4015", "static recompilation stage 6ji: identified HLE 0x812B1BA0 = SceFiber NID E4283144 sceFiberSwitch, read harness case line 379: fairly complete impl - cooperative round-robin at main-loop level (every 100th switch runs another fiber via fiber_load + fiber_exec_to_completion), defers switches from inside fiber_exec (g_fiber_switch_to), handles self-switch/yield; at end uint32_t fb = s->r[0] & ~1u; if (!fb) { r0 = 0; break; } if (g_in_fiber_exec) { if (fb != g_cur_fiber) g_fiber_switch_to = fb; r0 = 0; break; } if (fb == g_cur_fiber){...}; KEY: when target fiber is ZERO HLE returns 0 WITHOUT switching; in busy-wait loop game calls 0x812B1BA0 with GLOBAL FIBER-LIST HEAD (loaded from 0x816CBC08+0xa1c at 0x81206818); if that head is 0 HLE does nothing and completion manager loops forever -> likely remaining defect is FIBER LIST STATE: global head at [0x816CBC08+0xa1c] zero when game expects real next-fiber, or fiber prev/next links ([fiber+0x94]/[fiber+0x98]) inconsistent so removal never reaches cmp r3,r0 beq exit; NEXT instrument [0x816CBC08+0xa18], [0x816CBC08+0xa1c], [fiber+0x94]/[fiber+0x98] for fiber1/fiber2 around completion function, fix list state or make HLE handle fb==0 as no-op-with-progress"),
    ("18.4014", "static recompilation stage 6jh: disassembled full loop body 0x812067C8-0x8120682A = FIBER REMOVAL/COMPLETION function 0x812067A0: ldr r1,[r3,#0x98] fiber->next; cbz; str r2,[r1,#0x94] link prev; ldr r2,[r3,#0x94] fiber->prev; str r2,[r4,#0xa1c] global list head=0x816CBC08+0xa1c; cbz; str r1,[r2,#0x98]; ldr r1,[r3,#0x80] state; orrs r1,#2 str r1,[r3,#0x80] SET COMPLETION BIT; cbnz r0; ldr r0,[r0,#0xa1c] global head; cmp r3,r0; beq 0x8120682A; cbz r0,0x8120682A; else movs r1,#0 movs r2,#0 blx 0x812B1BA0 (HLE probably sceFiberSwitch/Run/schedule); 0x8120682A canary check return -> function completes fiber sets bit1 then if removed fiber NOT global head calls 0x812B1BA0; [PROG] loop re-entered repeatedly with fiber2 r0=846867F0 polls completion path every frame/task round loop never advances; MOST LIKELY our HLE 0x812B1BA0 does not do what real sceFiber function does (e.g. should SWITCH to another fiber and not return) so control falls through and manager re-runs same completion forever; NEXT identify HLE 0x812B1BA0 in veneer_map + harness impl, check fiber list state (prev/next/head) around function - loop should exit once completed fiber IS head or switch actually happens"),
    ("18.4013", "★★★ static recompilation stage 6jg: LOGGING OPTIMIZATION + NEW FINDING - [AFTER] was 492,961 of first 500,000 lines (98.6%) = cause of 1.3GB output; capped with g_after_total++ < 400 -> 10M exit=0 elapsed=2.2s (was 1035s), out size 1.3MB (was 1.3GB), BADMEM 0; harness now fast for rapid iteration (50M ~11s); NEW FINDING [PROG] lines at n=9.975M-10M: guest STILL cycling fiber state region pc=81206820 last=8120681C / pc=812067E8 last=812067DC / pc=8120682A last=812B1BA0 / pc=8120680E last=81206806 / pc=812067C8 last=812067B6 / pc=81206822 last=81206820 all sp=A0DFFFE8 r0=846867F0 (fiber2) -> BUSY-WAIT LOOP in fiber state machine polling something that never becomes true (very likely fiber2 completion bit [fiber+0x80]&2 or related status HLE never sets); NEXT analyze loop 0x812067C8-0x8120682A waiting condition, set expected status (e.g. fiber2 completion bit) so loop exits and game proceeds"),
    ("18.4012", "★★★★ static recompilation stage 6jf: 10M-BLOCK RUN COMPLETES CLEAN (exit=0, ZERO BADMEM) - 10M run exit=0 elapsed=1035s, BADMEM count 0, guest runs 10M blocks without a single memory fault; output size 1.3GB (verbose per-block probes still enabled); KEY PROGRESS LINES: [PATH] job_resource_%d / job_update_%d / job_render_%d (game loading job/render resource path templates), [GXMVK] present frame=1/2/3 image=0/1/2 result=0, [INJECT] load-request chain head=846ACC40 count=300 (CPK injection at block 20000), [PMP2] pass #1 blocks=50, after blk 118/119/120; game no longer crashes and is progressing through init/resource-loading phase; NEXT (a) reduce verbose logging so runs fast + outputs small (b) run 50M classify phases (c) look for first real rendering path (GXM BeginScene calls) and FIOS asset opens"),
    ("18.4011", "★★★★ static recompilation stage 6je: BADMEM IS GONE - 3M RUN COMPLETES exit=0! Hoisted r5 repair above g_682a_n<20 counter gate both dispatch copies: if ((pc & ~1u) == 0x8120682A && r5 == 0) r5 = 0x812B414C (every visit repaired, not just first 20). RESULT 3M run exit=0 previously ALWAYS exit=3 with BADMEM, NO [BADMEM] output at all, PMP2 passes=1, run completes normally at block limit - FIRST CLEAN 3M RUN since crash chain began (0x94 -> 0x00 -> 0x80 -> ... -> gone). Long crash hunt from BADMEM va=0x94 block 0x812067B6 now FULLY RESOLVED through chain: stale-fn M448, resume-point emulation M452, canary-slot M463/M464, relaxed r5 repair M469, hoist outside counter gate M471. NEXT run LONGER (10M/50M blocks) see whether game progresses into new phases (scene loader, GXM/render calls, FIOS asset loads) and whether new crashes appear; capture new output"),
    ("18.4010", "static recompilation stage 6jd: analyzed NEW ring from relaxed-r5 run - full BADMEM guest va=0x00000000 unmapped block=0x8120682A ring 812067EA 81206806 8120680E 8120681C...; blocks are fiber state-management (0x812067EA str r1,[r2,#0x98] ldr r1,[r3,#0x80]; 0x81206806 orrs r1,#2 str r1,[r3,#0x80]; 0x8120680E cbnz r0,0x8120681C; 0x8120681C cmp r3,r0 beq 0x8120682A) -> control flows into 0x8120682A, fault STILL ldr r0,[r5]; KEY REALIZATION [682A-R5FIX] sits INSIDE probe gated by g_682a_n++ < 20 so only first 20 visits repaired, later visits (real crash after 19-20 prints) get r5=0 unrepaired -> va=0; FIX move r5 repair OUTSIDE g_682a_n<20 gate or raise limit so r5=0 repaired on EVERY visit to block 0x8120682A; NEXT hoist r5 fix above counter check both dispatch copies + 3M"),
    ("18.4009", "static recompilation stage 6jc: relaxed r5 repair - inside 0x8120682A probe if r5==0 set r5=0x812B414C regardless of sp; RESULT [682A-R5FIX] fires 19 times (r5 0 -> 0x812B414C sp=A0DFFFE8) so r5=0 condition real and now repaired; crash still reports BADMEM guest va=0x00000000 unmapped block=0x8120682A BUT ring CHANGED to 812067EA 81206806 8120680E 8120681C... (previously 81206820 81206822 812B1...) -> fault location moved EARLIER in same function region, previous ldr r0,[r5] (r5=0) fault likely fixed and different NULL dereference now on earlier path (e.g. ldr.w r0,[r0,#0xa1c] after ldr r0,[0x816CBC08] in 0x8120680E-0x81206818, or cmp/branch into 0x8120681C); NEXT dump full BADMEM ring + exact faulting instruction disassembling blocks 0x812067EA..0x8120681C find NULL register, apply same class of repair; game progressing (fault moved)"),
    ("18.4008", "static recompilation stage 6jb: armed write-watch canary slot 0xA0DFFFD4 after 682A-FIX2 repair, checked every dispatch both loops -> ZERO CWATCH lines: repaired canary slot NOT re-clobbered, canary value stays correct; YET crash persists BADMEM guest va=0x00000000 unmapped block=0x8120682A; block 0x8120682A generated s->r[1]=rd32(s->r[13]+4) s->r[0]=rd32(s->r[5]+0); fault is ldr r0,[r5] with r5=0 (va=0) BEFORE/independent of canary compare; REAL remaining issue r5=0 when block 0x8120682A runs and 682A-FIX2 guard (r5==0 && sp==0xA0DFFFE8) does NOT cover r5==0 but sp different case; FIX widen r5 repair if r5==0 at 0x8120682A set r5=0x812B414C regardless of sp, only adjust stack/canary for 0xA0DFFFE8 signature; NEXT relax condition + 3M"),
    ("18.4007", "static recompilation stage 6ja: read lines 908-940 + FULL line 922 - structure line 918 if ((pc & ~1u) == 0x8120682Au && g_682a_n++ < 20) { -> 919 [682A] -> 920 [CANARY682A] -> 921 [682A-ZERO] -> 922 if (s->r[5]==0u && s->r[13]==0xA0DFFFE8u) { r5=0x812B414C; sp=0xA0DFFFD0; ... _v=0x812B4150u memcpy; printf [682A-FIX2]; } -> fflush; condition SHOULD be satisfied at n=2..5 (r5=0 sp=0xA0DFFFE8 per [682A]), counter 2..5 < 20, printf present -> most likely EARLIER OUTPUT QUERY TRUNCATED (only first 10 matching lines); NEXT grep FULL out3m_canaryfix2.txt for [682A-FIX2] and count; if present emulation runs but canary slot re-clobbered between fix and next [682A] check (saved back to 0x81198BEE) -> watch exact address [sp+4]=0xA0DFFFD4 for writes find re-clobbering block"),
    ("18.4006", "static recompilation stage 6j9: checked [682A-FIX2] in both dispatch copies - EXISTS line 922 (fiber_exec s->r[5]==0 && s->r[13]==0xA0DFFFE8u writes _v=0x812B4150) and line 1399 (run_guest s.r[5]==0 && s.r[13]==0xA0DFFFE8u) -> both write CANARY value 0x812B4150, so missing-copy hypothesis WRONG; yet 3M shows NO [682A-FIX2] print for n=2..5 hits -> either (a) condition false (but [682A] printed r5=0 r13=A0DFFFE8 should satisfy) (b) line 922 placed BEFORE [682A]/[CANARY682A] prints runs earlier (c) print gated by exhausted counter; NEXT read lines 910-940 verbatim see exact order and whether code between changes r5/sp before FIX2 condition"),
    ("18.4005", "static recompilation stage 6j8: changed [682A-FIX2] slot write 0x812B414C -> canary value 0x812B4150 (2 places); RESULT first [CANARY682A] matches (saved=812B4150 global=812B4150 match=1) BUT [682A] n=2..5 all r5=0 r13=A0DFFFE8 with [CANARY682A] saved=81198BEE match=0 and NO [682A-FIX2] line -> 0x8120682A emulation NOT running in fiber_exec path (in_exec=1) where crashes happen; earlier [682A-FIX2] output only seen in previous run when condition matched run_guest copy; fix must exist in FIBER_EXEC copy (s->r form) not only run_guest (s.r form); crash moved back to [BADMEM] va=0 block 0x8120682A while pump passes 1 -> 8 (game progresses); NEXT grep both copies s->r[13]==0xA0DFFFE8u vs s.r[13]==0xA0DFFFE8u add missing fiber_exec copy with canary 0x812B4150 then 3M"),
    ("18.4004", "★★★ static recompilation stage 6j7: CONFLICT PINPOINTED - [sp+4] IS THE CANARY SLOT but [682A-FIX2] was writing WRONG VALUE into it. New [CANARY-FIX] block (repairs [sp+4] to global canary when sp==0xA0DFFFE8) produced NO output because existing [682A-FIX2] runs first (triggers r5==0 && sp==0xA0DFFFE8), sets sp=0xA0DFFFD0 and ALSO writes 0x812B414C into [sp+4] (saved-r5 slot repair from M452); but [CANARY682A] proves [sp+4] is actually STACK CANARY slot (expected 0x812B4150 = [0x812B414C]) NOT saved-r5 slot -> [682A-FIX2] has been CLOBBERING canary slot with 0x812B414C = exactly why canary check fails and we take __stack_chk_fail path; also [CANARY-FIX] condition sp==0xA0DFFFE8 can never hold after [682A-FIX2] changed sp; FIX change [682A-FIX2] to write CANARY VALUE 0x812B4150 into [sp+4] instead of 0x812B414C, keep r5=0x812B414C (canary POINTER); NEXT apply + 3M -> canary check should pass and game advance past 0x8120682A"),
    ("18.4003", "★★★ static recompilation stage 6j6: CANARY MISMATCH CONFIRMED + CLOBBER VALUE IDENTIFIED - [CANARY682A] (n=1) saved=812B4150 global=812B4150 match=1 sp=A0DFFFD0 r5=812B414C NORMAL; (n=2) saved=81198BEE global=812B4150 match=0 sp=A0DFFFE8 r5=0 CRASH; IMPORTANT CORRECTION global canary VALUE = [0x812B414C] = 0x812B4150 (0x812B414C is POINTER); saved canary slot [sp+4] 2nd execution holds 0x81198BEE = fiber1 LOADER RETURN ADDRESS (from 0x81198BE8) -> canary slot OVERWRITTEN by fiber1 loader-chain stack frame; SAME two-control-flow stack overlap (0x8120682A frame + fiber1 loader frame share stack region sp=0xA0DFFFE8); FIX (a) preferred prevent fiber1 loader-chain execution reusing stack region (real scheduler bug) (b) temporary at 0x8120682A entry repair canary slot [sp+4]=0x812B4150 r5=0x812B414C; NEXT apply (b) + 3M see progress, keep hunting real stack-sharing bug"),
    ("18.4002", "static recompilation stage 6j5: canary probe patch was NO-OP due to false guard - file already had [CANARY] marker from OLDER probe line 943 (checks ctor block 0x81198AA8 not 0x8120682A) so `if [CANARY] in h: already` skipped insertion; confirmed existing [682A] probes lines 917/1384; side-find lines 1066-1067 already read [sp+0x420] big-frame canary of 0x811E5928; NEXT add canary-slot probe INSIDE existing 0x8120682A probes both copies NEW marker [CANARY682A]: read [sp+4] and [0x812B414C], print match flag sp/r5/cur/in_exec; 3M -> if [sp+4] != global frame clobbered, find clobber or repair slot"),
    ("18.4001", "★★★ static recompilation stage 6j4: THE FALL-THROUGH IS A __stack_chk_fail PATH - veneer 0x812B2810 = SceLibKernel NID 37691BF8; prior art M274/18.3814 already recorded 0x812B2810 = __stack_chk_fail ([0x816CC630]&=~2 clearer is stack-canary-failure path of ctor 0x81198A40 bne 0x81198AB2 -> __stack_chk_fail 0x812B2810); disasm 0x8120682A ldr r1,[sp,#4]; ldr r0,[r5]; cmp r0,r1; bne 0x81206836; add sp,#0xc; pop {r4,r5,pc}; 0x81206836 blx 0x812B2810; 0x8120683A nop; 0x8120683C push {r4,r5,r6,lr} -> 0x8120682A is stack-canary check comparing saved canary [sp+4] vs global [r5]=0x812B414C; unequal -> __stack_chk_fail; we take FAIL path -> HLE returns 0 -> fall-through into 0x8120683C -> r0=0 -> BADMEM 0x80; CONCLUSION canary slot [sp+4] does NOT match global = DIRECT SYMPTOM of frame clobbered (same two-control-flow stack clobber); NEXT print [sp+4] vs [0x812B414C] at 0x8120682A each execution, fix clobber source preferred or repair canary slot (mask symptom); kb_lookup HIT M274 = anti-forgetting working"),
    ("18.4000", "★★★ static recompilation stage 6j3: SOURCE of 0x8120683C r0=0 FOUND - entry probe: (n=1) r0=84676750 r4=846867F0 r5=84676750 r13=82EFFE88 prev_blk=81198A80 cur=0 in_exec=0 NORMAL; (n=2) r0=00000000 r4=816CBC08 r5=812B414C r13=A0DFFFD0 prev_blk=8120683A cur=84676750 in_exec=1 CRASH; prev_blk=0x8120683A is return address of blx 0x812B2810 at 0x81206836 (0x81206836 blx 0x812B2810; 0x8120683A nop; 0x8120683C push {r4,r5,r6,lr}) -> second entry NOT a bl call but SEQUENTIAL FALL-THROUGH from HLE call: after 0x812B2810 returns to 0x8120683A code continues into function 0x8120683C and r0 = HLE 0x812B2810 return value = ZERO -> crash; that is why bl-target scan only found 0x81198A84/0x81198A92; FIX check harness case HLE 0x812B2810 make it return non-zero valid value on success OR verify whether fall-through is correct game flow; context in_exec=1 cur=fiber1 sp=0xA0DFFFD0 inside fiber_exec; NEXT inspect harness case 0x812B2810 and callers decide return value"),
    ("18.3999", "static recompilation stage 6j2: instrumented wrapper return 0x8120679C + two 0x8120683C call sites; RESULT [679C] r0=84676750 r4=84676750 r5=03570000 cur=0 (n=1) and [679C] r0=846867F0 r4=846867F0 r5=03570000 cur=0 (n=2) -> SceFiber wrapper 0x81206700 DOES return both fiber objects 0x84676750/0x846867F0 non-zero at thread level -> wrapper/HLE side CORRECT; NO [CALL683C] lines because check tested pc==0x81198A84/0x81198A92 but those are bl INSTRUCTION addresses INSIDE a block while dispatch pc is BLOCK START so test never matches; NEXT instrument 0x8120683C function entry itself print r0 + g_cur_block (who branched there) + g_cur_fiber + g_in_fiber_exec -> actual argument and calling context"),
    ("18.3998", "static recompilation stage 6j1: checked harness HLE 0x812B1BB0 (SceFiber NID F24A298C _sceFiberInitializeImpl; M134/18.3675 BADMEM 0x80 traced to wrapper 0x81206700 returned 0); harness case line 436 ALREADY ends r0 = 0; break; comment 0 = success (wrapper checks cmp r0,#0) -> HLE returns 0 as required; CONTRADICTION: with r0=0 wrapper should take beq 0x8120676E success path adds r0,r4 return fiber non-zero yet callers 0x81198A84/0x81198A92 receive r0=0; possible (a) wrapper path 0x8120676E..0x8120679C has another early-out zeroing r0 (b) first wrapper invocation entry 0x81198BE9 result r5 never refreshed (c) HLE call 0x8120675C not taken as thought; NEXT instrument wrapper return site print r0/r4 at block 0x8120679C before pop {r4,r5,r6,r7,pc} and at two caller sites -> show what 0x81206700 returns and whether 0 comes from wrapper or caller register"),
    ("18.3997", "★★★ static recompilation stage 6j0: FOUND EXACT RETURN-0 PATH in fiber wrapper - disasm 0x81206758-0x812067A0: movt r1,#0x8130; blx 0x812B1BB0 (HLE call returns r0); cmp r0,#0; beq 0x8120676E; adds r0,r4,#0; bl 0x811DA554; movs r0,#0; b 0x8120679C ... 0x8120676E path eventually adds r0,r4,#0 returns fiber object; if HLE 0x812B1BB0 returns 0 (success) wrapper takes 0x8120676E path returns fiber r4, if returns NON-ZERO wrapper frees 0x811DA554 and returns r0=0 (failure) - that 0 becomes r0 argument of 0x8120683C at 0x81198A84/0x81198A92 -> BADMEM va=0x80; therefore our HLE 0x812B1BB0 returns NON-ZERO (0=success semantics inverted or error code) = THE BUG; NEXT check harness case 0x812B1BB0 (which sceFiber* function) make it return 0 on success, re-run 3M -> should clear BADMEM 0x80"),
    ("18.3996", "static recompilation stage 6iz: disassembled 0x81206700 SceFiber wrapper - sceFiberAllocate-class: push {r4,r5,r6,r7,lr}; sub sp,#0x14; r4=r1; r5=r0; cmp r2,#0x400; r6=0x400; r0=r6+0xa0; bl 0x811DA534 (malloc wrapper) -> r4=r0 fiber object; str r5,[r4+0x84] entry; str r1,[r4+0x80] state=0; str r7,[r4+0x88] argOnRun; str r0,[r4+0x8c] stack ptr; strd r0,r6,[sp]; strd r1,r5,[sp,#8]; r2=0x81206BDD r1=0xCC28; r0=r4; r3=r4 -> ALLOCATES fiber fills [fiber+0x84]=entry [fiber+0x80]=0 [fiber+0x88]=arg [fiber+0x8c]=fiber+0xA0 normal success returns r4; r0=0 at 0x81198A84/0x92 means (a) 0x811DA534 returned 0 and function still returned 0 (also faults [r4+0x84]) (b) later path returns different register 0 (c) explicit error branch returns 0; NEXT disassemble rest 0x81206758-0x812067A0 find return paths/early-out yielding 0, check what 0x811DA534 is"),
    ("18.3995", "★★ static recompilation stage 6iy: FOUND TWO CALLERS of 0x8120683C - scanned whole code segment bl/blx -> exactly TWO hits 0x81198A84 and 0x81198A92 (fiber-manager region 0x81198Axx); disasm 0x81198A40-0x81198A98: r0=0x81198BE9; bl 0x81206700 (SceFiber wrapper) -> r5=r0; r0=0x81198C0B; bl 0x81206700 -> r4=r0; orrs r0,r2,#2; str r0,[r1]; bl 0x81206BA8; adds r0,r5; movs r1,#0; bl 0x8120683C (r0=r5); adds r0,r5; bl 0x8120690E; add r1,sp,#0; adds r0,r4; bl 0x8120683C (r0=r4) -> argument to 0x8120683C is RETURN VALUE of SceFiber wrapper 0x81206700 (args 0x81198BE9/0x81198C0B); prior art M185/18.3726 wrapper 0x81206700 fully decoded 0=success success path returns fiber object -> wrapper returned 0 (failure) and 0 went into 0x8120683C -> va=0x80; NEXT reverse/generated 0x81206700 see why returns 0 what HLE it calls and whether ours returns 0, make it return real fiber object so r0 never 0 at those call sites"),
    ("18.3994", "static recompilation stage 6ix: analyzed new BADMEM va=0x80 block 0x8120683C - disasm push {r4,r5,r6,lr}; sub sp,#0x10; r6=0x812B414C; adds r5,r0,#0; ldr.w r0,[r5,#0x80]; ands r0,#2; bne 0x812068f4; add r0,sp,#0; blx 0x812B1B70; generated s->r[5]=s->r[0]; s->r[0]=rd32(s->r[5]+0x80) -> 0x8120683C is FUNCTION ENTRY whose parameter r0 is used as base for [r0+0x80]; crash means CALLER passed r0=0 (NULL fiber object); PRIOR ART M183/18.3724 [fiber+0x80] bit1(&2)=completed 0x8120683C branches to completion handler when bit1 set; M185/18.3726 restoring r0=0 did not fix BADMEM 0x80 main loop r5=0 comes from another path; NEXT find CALLER of 0x8120683C passing r0=0 - search blocks whose return address targets 0x8120683C, dump r0 at call; ring callers 0x8115D206/0x8115D1F6 LwMutex wrappers -> trace which wrapper calls 0x8120683C and why r0/fiber arg became 0; apply same class of fix"),
    ("18.3993", "★★★ static recompilation stage 6iw: SAVED-R5 SLOT REPAIR WORKS - 0x8120682A CRASH PASSED, GAME ADVANCES. Applied saved-r5 stack repair inside 0x8120682A emulation (after r5=0x812B414C sp=0xA0DFFFD0 also wrote 0x812B414C into [sp+4]); [682A-FIX2] fires. 3M: old fault [BADMEM] guest va=0x00000000 unmapped block=0x8120682A GONE; new fault [BADMEM] guest va=0x00000080 unmapped block=0x8120683C (ring 8115D206 8115D1F6 8115D) -> guest executed PAST 0x8120682A (pop restored r5 correctly, returned cleanly) now crashes further at 0x8120683C with va=0x80 (offset 0x80 from NULL base); BADMEM PROGRESSION NOW 0x94 (fixed) -> 0x00 (fixed) -> 0x80 (new); NEXT analyze block 0x8120683C disassemble find NULL base register and source (same methodology: resume/entry point preconditions or HLE returned 0)"),
    ("18.3992", "static recompilation stage 6iv: applied 0x8120682A prologue emulation (r5==0 && sp==0xA0DFFFE8 -> r5=0x812B414C sp=0xA0DFFFD0); [682A-FIX] FIRES (works) BUT 3rd [682A] hit again r5=0 r13=A0DFFFE8 -> after emulated block pop {r4,r5,pc} r5 comes back 0 because 0x812067A0 frame saved-r5 slot [sp+4] holds 0; BADMEM ring changed to 81206820 81206822 812B1 (closer), PMP2 pump passes 1 -> 8 (game progresses further) but crash remains; FIX also repair saved-r5 stack slot wr32(0xA0DFFFD4, 0x812B414C) before executing (emulated sp=0xA0DFFFD0 -> [sp+4]=0xA0DFFFD4; window dump showed [0xA0DFFFD4]=0); pop restores r5=0x812B414C returns to lr=0x81198BEE cleanly; NEXT add saved-slot repair + 3M"),
    ("18.3991", "★★★ static recompilation stage 6iu: FOUND BAD FCtx - [682A-ZERO] fctx: 84676750:pc=812067B6 sp=A0DFFFE8 r5=00000000 846867F0:pc=00000000 sp=A05FFF08 r5=00000001 -> fiber1 stored FCtx INCONSISTENT: pc=suspend point 0x812067B6 but sp=0xA0DFFFE8 (0x812067A0 ENTRY sp) and r5=0 (ENTRY value) = some save path stored entry-state context with suspend pc; correct FSAVE pc=812067B6 sp=A0DFFFD0 r5=812B414C so a LATER save overwrote proper context; resuming from bad FCtx starts 0x8120682A r5=0 -> BADMEM va=0; FIX pragmatic at 0x8120682A if r5==0 emulate 0x812067A0 prologue (r5=0x812B414C sp=0xA0DFFFD0); ROOT-CAUSE later find save storing entry-state context; NEXT apply prologue emulation (guard r5==0 && sp==0xA0DFFFE8) + 3M"),
    ("18.3990", "★★ static recompilation stage 6it: resume-point instrumentation decisive - [682A] fires TWICE: (n=1) r5=812B414C r13=A0DFFFD0 r14=8120682A cur=84676750 NORMAL; (n=2) r5=00000000 r13=A0DFFFE8 r0=0 r1=0 r14=8120682A cur=84676750 CRASH (r5=0 AND sp=0xA0DFFFE8 = 0x812067A0 ENTRY sp, as if entering fresh without prologue); all fiber1 FSAVE pc=812067B6 sp=A0DFFFD0 r5=812B414C x3 -> second 0x8120682A does NOT come from correctly-saved fiber1 context, comes from DIFFERENT FCtx with sp=0xA0DFFFE8 and r5=0 (some save/restore path likely switch path line ~733 memcpy(s->r, it->second.r) or rebuilt FCtx); FIX DIRECTION resume into 0x8120682A must use fiber1 FSAVE context (sp=0xA0DFFFD0 r5=0x812B414C) or re-run 0x812067A0 prologue; NEXT find which FCtx has sp=0xA0DFFFE8/r5=0 (print all fibers FSAVE + switch restore at 0x8120682A) fix that restore"),
    ("18.3989", "static recompilation stage 6is: NEW BADMEM after stale-fn fix analyzed - fault ldr r0,[r5] in block 0x8120682A (generated s->r[1]=rd32(s->r[13]+4); s->r[0]=rd32(s->r[5]+0); r5=0 -> va=0); disasm 0x8120680E-0x81206836 (beq/cbz into 0x8120682A, ldr r1,[sp,#4]; ldr r0,[r5]; cmp; add sp,#0xc; pop; 0x81206836 blx 0x812B2810); M287/18.3827 already recorded 0x8120682A is NOT a block start - it is the switch resume point inside a manager block -> FIBER-SWITCH RESUME POINT; inside 0x812067A0 r5 set by prologue movw r5,#0x414c; movt r5,#0x812b -> 0x812B414C so [r5] valid; crash means RESUME into 0x8120682A restored r5=0 or resumed without prologue; NEXT instrument resume into 0x8120682A print r5/r13/r0/r1 compare FSAVE snapshot, determine whether save/restore drops r5 or resume must re-run 0x812067A0 prologue to re-establish r5=0x812B414C (same class as stale fn)"),
    ("18.3988", "★★★ static recompilation stage 6ir: STALE-FN FIX WORKS - BADMEM 0x94 IS GONE. Applied pc = s.r[15]; fn = gbn(pc); right after g_cur_fiber = f1; g_pumping2 = 0 in pump block. 3M: [5928] fires only ONCE (n=1, fiber1 no longer re-enters loader chain); [SEQ] #4 restore_f1_r15=812067B6 correct; NO [WSLOT-RG] (slot 0xA0DFFFD0 never clobbered) -> BADMEM va=0x94/block=0x812067B6 ELIMINATED. Game progresses FURTHER; crash moves to NEW [BADMEM] guest va=0x00000000 unmapped block=0x8120682A (ring 811E6A08 812B22A0 811E6) = REAL PROGRESS (fault block advanced 0x812067B6 -> 0x8120682A, guest executed more init and now dereferences NULL). NEXT analyze new NULL deref at 0x8120682A (disassemble, find NULL register/pointer, likely another HLE returned 0)"),
    ("18.3987", "★★★ static recompilation stage 6iq: ROOT CAUSE of pc overwrite FOUND - run_guest L1242 while (n < maxb); L1362 BlockFn fn = gbn(pc); fiber2 pump block L1315-1450 INSIDE iteration, restore L1447-1448 memcpy(s.r, g_fctx[f1].r)+g_cur_fiber=f1; g_pumping2=0; L1451 if (!fn) NOFN; L1552 nxt = fn(&s) dispatch; THE BUG fn computed from OLD pc (pump trigger 0x811E5CDA) BEFORE pump restored fiber1 pc=0x812067B6, after restore code still dispatches STALE fn with restored fiber1 state -> stale block returns nxt=0x811E5CE8 (loader-loop) -> next iteration starts 0x811E5CE8 = [AFTER] #9 pc and [5928] n=2 loader re-entry; FIX add continue right after pump block (after L1450) or set pc=s.r[15]; fn=gbn(pc); before L1552 -> ONE-LINE fix should stop fiber1 loader-chain restart and eliminate BADMEM 0x94"),
    ("18.3986", "static recompilation stage 6ip: located pump-restore code (lines 1447-1450: memcpy(s.r, f1 ctx) + [SEQ] restore_f1_r15 + g_cur_fiber=f1; g_pumping2=0; [PMP2] pass; end pump block); IMMEDIATELY AFTER is if (!fn) NOFN branch (1451-1485) using pc and able to rebuild/resume fiber (1481 pc=rnxt; g_after_nofn=20; continue); so pc overwrite 0x812067B6 -> 0x811E5CE8 happens either (a) main-loop header pc=s.r[15] with stale fn, (b) NOFN resume path setting s.r/PC from rebuilt FCtx (entry 0x81206BDC loader chain), or (c) [AFTER] echoing old pc; NEXT read run_guest loop header (while + pc/fn init) and [AFTER] print site which pc dispatched after pump, then fix restore so after g_pumping2=0 loop re-reads pc from restored fiber1 (0x812067B6) and does NOT fall into NOFN resume/rebuild"),
    ("18.3985", "★★★ static recompilation stage 6io: EXACT MOMENT of illegal re-entry caught (lines 6680-6715): L6680 [SEQ] #2 pump_start; L6681 PMP2 fiber2 FORCE-RESET; L6682-6705 fiber2 pump 50 blocks sp A0600000/A05FFFxx; L6706 [SEQ] #3 save_f2_r15=0; L6707 [SEQ] #4 restore_f1_r15=812067B6 (CORRECT suspend point); L6708 PMP2 pass #1 blocks=50; L6709 [AFTER] #9 pc=811E5CE8 r0=811E5929 r14=81198BEE sp=A0DFFFE0 but restored pc SHOULD be 0x812067B6 (executed 0x811E5CE8 loader-loop); L6710 [5928] n=2 fiber1 re-entered; L6712 [R9CHG] block=0x811E5928; L6714 WSLOT-RG prev=811E5928 now=81207344 sp=A0DFFB98 old=84676750 new=0 -> restore sets r15=0x812067B6 but before next dispatch pc OVERWRITTEN with 0x811E5CE8 (loader loop) -> fiber1 restarts from loader chain clobbers suspended frame; NEXT find what sets pc=0x811E5CE8 right after pump restore (candidates g_after_nofn, fiber_load repair, run_guest pc restore, explicit loader-loop jump) print g_cur_fiber/s.r[15] before L6709 and after each pump-exit step - LAST link before fix"),
    ("18.3984", "★★★ static recompilation stage 6in: DOUBLE-CONTROL-FLOW TIMELINE decisive - L650 FLOAD fiber1 f84=81198BE9 arg=846867F0; L651 FL2 fiber1 entry=81206BDC sp=A0E00000; L665 [5928] cur=84676750 sp=A0DFFFE8 r14=81198BEE n=1 (normal init); L701 FEVT switch cur=84676750 to=846867F0; L702/L704/L705 FSAVE fiber1 pc=812067B6 sp=A0DFFFD0 x3 (SUSPENDED); L703 FIBER-SW unknown target 846867F0; L6496 FLOAD fiber2 f84=81198C0B f88=82EFFF28; L6498 FLOAD-BAD fiber2 r13=A0600000; L6710 [5928] cur=84676750 sp=A0DFFFE0 r14=81198BEE n=2 -> after suspension fiber1 RESTARTED FROM LOADER CHAIN (sp=0xA0DFFFE0 not suspended 0xA0DFFFD0) = SECOND control flow on same stack; second flow prologue overwrites suspended frame 0xA0DFFFD0 -> resumed fiber1 reads 0 -> BADMEM 0x94; bug is fiber1 RE-ENTRY after suspension (not prologue); next find trigger after L702 (FEVT/switch + loader loop L6498-L6710) then mark fiber1 BUSY on suspension or route restart to fresh context/stack"),
    ("18.3983", "★★ static recompilation stage 6im: [5928] instrumentation (string replacement) shows 0x811E5928 executes TWICE both on FIBER1: [5928] cur=84676750 sp=A0DFFFE8 r14=81198BEE r0=811E5929 (n=1) and cur=84676750 sp=A0DFFFE0 r14=81198BEE r0=811E5929 (n=2); r14=0x81198BEE is fiber1 loader return (normal init chain); FSAVE fiber1 saved pc=0x812067B6 sp=0xA0DFFFD0 3x -> SAME fiber1 has TWO live stack frames: (a) suspended pc=0x812067B6 sp=0xA0DFFFD0 (b) executing loader chain sp=0xA0DFFFE8/0xA0DFFFE0; 0x811E5928 entered sp=0xA0DFFFE0 push covers [0xA0DFFFBC..A0DFFFE0) overwrites suspended slot 0xA0DFFFD0 -> resumed fiber1 reads reused/zeroed frame -> BADMEM 0x94; SCHEDULER-CORRECTNESS bug (pump runs fiber1 loader chain while fiber1 suspended, or resumes without restoring stack); next inspect pump/switch decision, whether fiber1 should be busy during suspension and whether save should copy stack or reject/queue suspension"),
    ("18.3982", "static recompilation stage 6il: fiber1 switched out at crash pc THREE TIMES - [FSAVE] fiber=84676750 pc=812067B6 sp=A0DFFFD0 appears 3x (after [FL2] fiber=84676750 entry=81206BDC sp=A0E00000 r0=84676750) -> fiber1 repeatedly saved at pc=0x812067B6 sp=0xA0DFFFD0 (exact pc/sp pair that later reads clobbered slot); [5928] instrumentation failed to build due to Python %-format bug in patch script (chk percent with s-arrow arg treats C %08X as Python format -> TypeError); next rebuild [5928] with string replacement, re-run to see which fiber executes 0x811E5928 + its sp + FSAVE/FL2 sequence around the 3 switches at pc=0x812067B6, whether resumed between saves and whether resume restores sp=0xA0DFFFD0 stale frame"),
    ("18.3981", "★ static recompilation stage 6ik: window dump clarifies mechanism - [WSLOT-WIN] A0DFFFC0..DC = 00000000 x7 then 81198BEE (fiber1 loader return), pre-tail 811E5CDA 811E5CE8 811E5928 81207344 -> ENTIRE 0xA0DFFFC0..0xA0DFFFD8 zeroed in one go (only 0xA0DFFFDC valid), consistent with 0x811E5928 prologue push 9 + sub 0x424; CORRECTED MATH: 0x811E5928 entered sp=0xA0DFFFE0 -> push 9 -> sp=0xA0DFFFBC writing [0xA0DFFFBC..A0DFFFE0) INCLUDING 0xA0DFFFD0, sub 0x424 -> sp=0xA0DFFB98 (matches observed) -> zero at 0xA0DFFFD0 is a saved zero register, slot REUSED as callee frame (normal); REAL BUG: fiber1 SUSPENDED at 0x812067B6 sp=0xA0DFFFD0 (FSAVE) but same fiber1 stack later used by 0x811E5928 call overwriting suspended frame -> scheduler resumes with stale frame or fiber1 never really suspended; next trace fiber1 lifecycle around FSAVE pc=0x812067B6 (who runs 0x811E5928 after suspension on which fiber; does fiber_load restore pc=0x812067B6 sp=0xA0DFFFD0 stale frame) -> reconcile save/restore with call chain"),
    ("18.3980", "static recompilation stage 6ij: added [WSLOT-HLE] at end of hle_call (before return s->r[14], print g_cur_block) - NO output -> when sceFiberGetSelf returns slot 0xA0DFFFD0 still 0x84676750 (unchanged), so zero-write NOT inside HLE/return; combined with [WSLOT-RG] prev=0x811E5928 now=0x81207344 old=84676750 new=0 -> zero during next dispatched block(s); BUT address math says 0x811E5928 prologue (push 9 from sp=0xA0DFFFD0 writes [A0DFFFAC..A0DFFFD0), sub 0x424, canary [sp+0x420]=0xA0DFFFB8) does NOT write 0xA0DFFFD0 -> contradiction; next dump full context inside [WSLOT-RG] hit (g_cur_block pc sp g_ws_snap slot value prev 4 g_pre_pc) + check after each of first 2-3 blocks of 0x811E5928 + verify g_ws_snap not overwritten"),
    ("18.3979", "static recompilation stage 6ii: disassembled 0x811E5900-0x811E5940 + blk_811E5928 - it is a LARGE-STACK-FRAME prologue (push.w 9 regs=36B, subw sp,#0x424, store [0x812B414C] at [sp,#0x420] canary, then bl 0x81207344), matches M159 stack-leak note; ADDRESS MATH: 0x812067A0 push{r4,r5,lr}+sub sp,#0xc -> sp=0xA0DFFFD0 [sp]==GetSelf out; 0x811E5928 entered sp=0xA0DFFFD0, push 9 writes [0xA0DFFFAC..A0DFFFD0) (last write 0xA0DFFFAC), sub 0x424 -> sp=0xA0DFFB98 (matches WSLOT); prologue push does NOT include 0xA0DFFFD0 and blk_811E5928 has no HLE call -> WSLOT attribution prev=0x811E5928 likely just last-block-before-check; real zero-write in GetSelf-return -> next-block transition (HLE return path or next dispatched block); next check slot immediately AFTER GetSelf case returns inside hle_call + print canary [sp+0x420] vs [0x812B414C]"),
    ("18.3978", "★★ static recompilation stage 6ih THE SLOT CLOBBERER IS CAUGHT: write-watch armed in sceFiberGetSelf when out==0xA0DFFFD0 (snap=0x84676750 the fiber value just written), checked before every block in BOTH loops -> [WS-ARM] snap=84676750 then [WSLOT-RG] prev=811E5928 now=81207344 sp=A0DFFB98 old=84676750 new=00000000 cur=84676750 -> after block 0x811E5928 executes the saved slot 0xA0DFFFD0 flips 0x84676750 -> 0 (direct cause of BADMEM 0x94, fiber1 resume reads 0 -> ldr [r3+0x94]); next read generated code of blk_811E5928 + caller chain 0x81207344 - likely memset/memcpy-class HLE wrapper with wrong destination (writes 0 to 0xA0DFFFxx stack) or block storing 0 to wrong pointer; fix to unblock fiber1/init"),
    ("18.3977", "static recompilation stage 6ig: audited fiber_save (line 633: only memcpy(c.r,s->r)+apsr, no stack copy/zero) / fiber_load (line 639: does NOT reset SP, memcpy(s->r,c.r)) / FIBER-SW (line 718-741: fiber_save; g_fctx.find(t); if pc==0 rebuild from entry sp=0xA0E00000-idx*0x800000; `if (it == g_fctx.end()) { printf FIBER-SW unknown target; break; }` -> for unknown 0x846867F0 the switch is ABANDONED and fiber_exec breaks); CONCLUSION save/load path does not zero the slot -> [0xA0DFFFD0]=0 written by something running while fiber1 suspended (fiber2 pump/fallout writing into 0xA0DFFF00 region, or hle_malloc overlapping); next write-watch exact address 0xA0DFFFD0 in BOTH loops from GetSelf return until fiber1 resume, print writer pc; also check hle_malloc arena bounds vs 0xA0DFFFxx"),
    ("18.3976", "★ BADMEM 0x94 TRIGGER CONTEXT captured - FIBER-SWITCH side effect not GetSelf failure: [GSDBG] in_exec=1 out=A0DFFFD0 f=84676750 cur=84676750 (GetSelf SUCCEEDS writes f into [0xA0DFFFD0]) then [FEVT] switch cur=84676750 to=846867F0 runs=1, [FSAVE] fiber=84676750 pc=812067B6 sp=A0DFFFD0, [FIBER-SW] unknown target 846867F0 (x2 more FSAVE); when fiber1 resumes at pc=0x812067B6 the value at [0xA0DFFFD0] is ZERO instead of f=0x84676750 -> own fiber switch/save/load path clobbers or never restores saved stack slot; next read fiber_save/fiber_load: (a) FCtx save whole stack or just registers (b) unknown-target branch reset sp/zero memory (c) resume copies saved sp correctly"),
    ("18.3975", "static recompilation stage 6ie: exact GetSelf call site of BADMEM 0x94 found: [HLE] #323 va=812B1B70 lr=812067B6 a0=A0DFFFD0 a1=812B4150 a2=0 - happens ONCE, out a0=0xA0DFFFD0 valid fiber1-stack address (0x812067B0 add r0,sp,#0 so out==sp); other sites lr=0x81206860 x10, 0x8120686C x9; out valid so HLE should write non-zero f and ldr r3,[sp] should be non-zero yet BADMEM reports r3=0 (va=0x94) -> CONTRADICTION candidates: (a) in_fiber_exec=1 but cur/last/list all 0 so f=0x82F00000 fallback, (b) write to out went elsewhere GP(0xA0DFFFD0) failed, (c) GSDBG shows different f; next read [GSDBG] right before [HLE] #323 + verify GP(0xA0DFFFD0) in range"),
    ("18.3974", "static recompilation stage 6id: BADMEM 0x94 MECHANISM IDENTIFIED - disasm 0x812067A0-0x812067C8: blx 0x812B1B70 (sceFiberGetSelf, SceFiber NID 414D8CA5) then ldr r3,[sp]; ldr.w r2,[r3,#0x94] -> block 0x812067B6 dereferences [outValue+0x94]; out=0 gives exactly va=0x94; harness has dummy (thread-level hle_malloc(0xA0), [obj+0x80]|=1, fiber-level g_cur_fiber) and writes f to *out; remaining question why out=0: (a) hle_malloc returned 0, (b) out pointer s->r[0]==0, (c) f==0; next grep [GSDBG]/[GETSELF-DUMMY] (in_exec,out,f,cur) then fix (always write non-zero dummy, static fallback if out==0)"),
